{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FT1BVor1hddKuvc4dTKEHv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Standard Operating Procedures\n     2→\n     3→This document captures the development conventions, release workflow, and operational norms for the Hankweave codebase. Written for humans and AI agents working in the repo.\n     4→\n     5→Last updated: 2026-02-14 (v0.4.1).\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## 1. Repository Structure\n    10→\n    11→```\n    12→hankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n    13→├── server/                 ← runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n    14→├── scripts/                ← build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n    15→├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n    16→├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n    17→├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n    18→├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n    19→├── intermediates/          ← planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n    20→├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n    21→├── public-release-files/   ← files overlaid onto the public repo during sync\n    22→├── assets/                 ← images, demo GIFs\n    23→├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n    24→├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n    25→├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n    26→└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm)\n    27→```\n    28→\n    29→There is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n    30→\n    31→### What gets stripped before public release\n    32→\n    33→The sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n    34→\n    35→- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`\n    36→- **Files**: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md` (root), `reference/telemetry.md` (internal version), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `.DS_Store`\n    37→\n    38→The `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements that get overlaid: a public-facing `README.md`, `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`, a sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`, and a simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n    39→\n    40→The `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, and `release:*` scripts are removed.\n    41→\n    42→---\n    43→\n    44→## 2. Branch Model\n    45→\n    46→```\n    47→feature branches → develop → release/alpha\n    48→                      ↑\n    49→              all PRs target here\n    50→```\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"6fc9c729-f78e-4e38-bf92-3038bb8a1982","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md","content":"# Standard Operating Procedures\n\nThis document captures the development conventions, release workflow, and operational norms for the Hankweave codebase. Written for humans and AI agents working in the repo.\n\nLast updated: 2026-02-14 (v0.4.1).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Repository Structure\n\n```\nhankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n├── server/                 ← runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n├── scripts/                ← build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n├── intermediates/          ← planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n├── public-release-files/   ← files overlaid onto the public repo during sync\n├── assets/                 ← images, demo GIFs\n├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm)\n```\n\nThere is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n\n### What gets stripped before public release\n\nThe sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n\n- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`\n- **Files**: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md` (root), `reference/telemetry.md` (internal version), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `.DS_Store`\n\nThe `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements that get overlaid: a public-facing `README.md`, `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`, a sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`, and a simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n\nThe `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, and `release:*` scripts are removed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Branch Model\n\n```\nfeature branches → develop → release/alpha\n                      ↑\n              all PRs target here\n```","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":406}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:29:32.649Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NCq8X86k2okWjXDJfHKN1H","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→name: 'Setup Environment'\n     2→description: 'Sets up Node.js, Bun, and project dependencies'\n     3→\n     4→inputs:\n     5→  install-gemini:\n     6→    description: 'Install gemini-cli globally'\n     7→    required: false\n     8→    default: 'true'\n     9→  codex-auth-json:\n    10→    description: 'Codex auth.json content for authentication (codex binary is bundled with @openai/codex-sdk)'\n    11→    required: false\n    12→    default: ''\n    13→  registry-url:\n    14→    description: 'Optional registry URL for npm publishing'\n    15→    required: false\n    16→    default: ''\n    17→\n    18→runs:\n    19→  using: 'composite'\n    20→  steps:\n    21→    - name: Setup Node.js\n    22→      uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n    23→      with:\n    24→        node-version: '20'\n    25→        registry-url: ${{ inputs.registry-url || '' }}\n    26→\n    27→    - name: Setup Bun\n    28→      uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@v2\n    29→      with:\n    30→        bun-version: latest\n    31→\n    32→    - name: Install dependencies\n    33→      shell: bash\n    34→      run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\n    35→\n    36→    - name: Install gemini-cli globally\n    37→      if: inputs.install-gemini == 'true'\n    38→      shell: bash\n    39→      run: npm install -g @google/gemini-cli\n    40→\n    41→    - name: Setup Codex authentication\n    42→      if: inputs.codex-auth-json != ''\n    43→      shell: bash\n    44→      run: |\n    45→        # Create ~/.codex directory\n    46→        mkdir -p ~/.codex\n    47→\n    48→        # Create auth.json from input (codex binary is bundled with @openai/codex-sdk package)\n    49→        echo '${{ inputs.codex-auth-json }}' > ~/.codex/auth.json\n    50→\n    51→        # Verify file was created (for debugging)\n    52→        if [ -f ~/.codex/auth.json ]; then\n    53→          echo \"✓ auth.json created successfully\"\n    54→        else\n    55→          echo \"✗ Failed to create auth.json\"\n    56→          exit 1\n    57→        fi\n    58→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"882643e8-7a19-477e-ab8e-a43d6c279979","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml","content":"name: 'Setup Environment'\ndescription: 'Sets up Node.js, Bun, and project dependencies'\n\ninputs:\n  install-gemini:\n    description: 'Install gemini-cli globally'\n    required: false\n    default: 'true'\n  codex-auth-json:\n    description: 'Codex auth.json content for authentication (codex binary is bundled with @openai/codex-sdk)'\n    required: false\n    default: ''\n  registry-url:\n    description: 'Optional registry URL for npm publishing'\n    required: false\n    default: ''\n\nruns:\n  using: 'composite'\n  steps:\n    - name: Setup Node.js\n      uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n      with:\n        node-version: '20'\n        registry-url: ${{ inputs.registry-url || '' }}\n\n    - name: Setup Bun\n      uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@v2\n      with:\n        bun-version: latest\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      shell: bash\n      run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\n\n    - name: Install gemini-cli globally\n      if: inputs.install-gemini == 'true'\n      shell: bash\n      run: npm install -g @google/gemini-cli\n\n    - name: Setup Codex authentication\n      if: inputs.codex-auth-json != ''\n      shell: bash\n      run: |\n        # Create ~/.codex directory\n        mkdir -p ~/.codex\n\n        # Create auth.json from input (codex binary is bundled with @openai/codex-sdk package)\n        echo '${{ inputs.codex-auth-json }}' > ~/.codex/auth.json\n\n        # Verify file was created (for debugging)\n        if [ -f ~/.codex/auth.json ]; then\n          echo \"✓ auth.json created successfully\"\n        else\n          echo \"✗ Failed to create auth.json\"\n          exit 1\n        fi\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:29:32.663Z"}
