{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KkNF8NSYuvcS7S6doKZ5gh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VRfcfmtbaGpbbbvZqVgnpM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/addendum-docs-and-deployment.md","content":"# Addendum: Documentation Site and Deployment\n\nRead alongside `plan.md`. Covers the docs workspace integration details, Vercel deployment migration, and cross-repo schema flow.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Documentation site structure\n\nThe docs site is a Nextra 4 + Next.js 15 application. It currently lives at `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` and will be flattened into `docs/` in the monorepo:\n\n```\ndocs/                               (was: hankweave-docs/nextra-site/)\n├── app/                            Next.js app directory (App Router)\n│   ├── layout.tsx                  Root layout with Navbar, Footer, PostHog analytics\n│   ├── posthog-provider.tsx        PostHog analytics wrapper (client-side)\n│   └── [[...mdxPath]]/page.tsx     Catch-all MDX route (Nextra 4 pattern)\n├── content/                        MDX documentation pages\n│   ├── _meta.ts                    Top-level navigation config\n│   ├── index.mdx                   Landing page\n│   ├── concepts/                   Core Concepts (codons, hanks, rigs, loops, etc.)\n│   ├── guides/                     Getting Started, Building, Testing, Debugging\n│   ├── reference/                  CLI, Config, API Keys, Protocol, etc.\n│   └── examples/                   Example hanks\n├── components/                     Custom React components (MobileSearchFab, etc.)\n├── public/                         Static assets\n│   ├── images/                     Logos, diagrams, screenshots\n│   └── schemas/                    JSON schemas (generated by runtime's generate-schemas.ts)\n├── styles/                         Global CSS\n├── mdx-components.tsx              MDX component overrides\n├── next-env.d.ts                   Next.js TypeScript declarations\n├── next.config.mjs                 Nextra + Next.js config\n├── package.json                    hankweave-docs v2.0.0\n├── tsconfig.json                   ES2020, bundler moduleResolution, strict: false\n└── vercel.json                     Framework: nextjs, bun install/build\n```\n\nImportant: The docs use Nextra 4 with App Router conventions. Content lives in `content/` (not `pages/`), and routes are defined via the catch-all `app/[[...mdxPath]]/page.tsx` pattern.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key observations from the docs source\n\n1. **No runtime imports.** The docs site does not import TypeScript modules from `@southbridgeai/hankweave`. It references hankweave as a CLI tool (`npx hankweave`, `bunx hankweave`) but doesn't use it as a library dependency. This means no `workspace:*` dependency is needed.\n\n2. **Schema hosting.** The `public/schemas/` directory hosts JSON schemas generated by the runtime's `generate-schemas.ts`. These are served as static files referenced from docs pages. This is the only data flow from runtime to docs.\n\n3. **Layout links to public repo.** `app/layout.tsx` links to `https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` as the project URL. This doesn't change -- the public mirror continues to be the user-facing repo.\n\n4. **PostHog analytics.** Client-side integration in `app/posthog-provider.tsx`. No migration impact.\n\n5. **Pagefind search.** The `postbuild` script runs `pagefind --site .next/server/app --output-path public/_pagefind`. This runs relative to the docs workspace directory and works in the monorepo. The generated `public/_pagefind/` directory needs to be in `.gitignore`.\n\n6. **TypeScript configs are incompatible.** Runtime: `target: ES2022`, `module: ES2022`, `moduleResolution: node`, `strict: true`, types: `bun-types`. Docs: `target: ES2020`, `module: esnext`, `moduleResolution: bundler`, `strict: false`, plugins: `next`. These configs must remain separate. Do not create a shared `tsconfig.base.json`.\n\n7. **Build environment variable.** The `vercel.json` contains `\"DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969\": \"1\"` in build env. This is specific to the Vercel build and stays in `docs/vercel.json` unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SOP updates needed\n\n### 3.1: Repository structure (Section 1, lines 10-27)\n\nReplace the directory tree with the version shown in Phase 5 of the plan. Add the note about docs being a workspace that deploys to Vercel.\n\n### 3.2: Strip list documentation (Section 1, lines 31-40)\n\nAdd `docs/` to the directories list. Add a note: \"The `package.json` transformation also removes the `\\\"workspaces\\\"` field to prevent the public repo from referencing the missing docs directory.\"\n\n### 3.3: Key files reference (Section 9, lines 337-354)\n\nAdd:\n```\n| `docs/package.json`         | Documentation site workspace (hankweave-docs)              |\n| `docs/content/`             | MDX documentation pages (concepts, guides, reference)      |\n```\n\n### 3.4: Development workflow (Section 3)\n\nAdd a \"Documentation site\" subsection describing how to run `bun run dev` and `bun run build` from `docs/`, and how `bun run generate-schemas` writes to both schema locations.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Documentation that should NOT be updated\n\n### User-facing docs (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`)\n\nThe docs cover concepts, guides, and reference material for hankweave users. None reference the repository structure. The monorepo migration is invisible to users.\n\n### Public README (`public-release-files/README.md`)\n\nDescribes the public mirror repo. The monorepo structure is not visible to public users.\n\n### CHANGELOG\n\nOptional -- can add an internal note under `[Unreleased] > Changed` but it's not user-facing.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Vercel deployment migration\n\n### Current state\n\nThe docs deploy from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs`. Vercel runs:\n1. `bun install` (as specified in `vercel.json`)\n2. `bun run build` (Next.js build + Pagefind postbuild)\n3. Deploy the `.next` output\n\n### Required changes\n\n**Step 1: Connect Vercel to the monorepo**\n1. Go to the Vercel project settings for hankweave-docs.\n2. Under \"Git\" -> \"Connected Git Repository\", change from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`.\n3. Set \"Root Directory\" to `docs`.\n4. Verify Framework Preset is \"Next.js\".\n\n**Step 2: Validate install behavior**\n\nWhen Vercel sets root to `docs/` and runs `bun install` there, Bun should detect it's a workspace member and look upward for the root `package.json`. If this works correctly, the full workspace dependency tree is installed using the root `bun.lock`.\n\nIf this fails (Vercel only mounts the subdirectory and Bun can't find the workspace root):\n- Set Vercel root directory to `/` (repo root)\n- Set install command to `bun install`\n- Set build command to `cd docs && bun run build`\n- Vercel will detect Next.js from the `docs/` directory\n\n**Step 3: Configure \"Ignored Build Step\" (recommended)**\n1. Go to Settings -> General -> \"Ignored Build Step\".\n2. Set to: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n\nThis prevents unnecessary rebuilds when only runtime code changes.\n\n**Step 4: Configure branch deployment**\n\nThe monorepo uses `develop` and `release/alpha` branches. Configure Vercel production and preview deployment branches according to team preference. Currently the docs repo likely deploys from `main` -- this changes to whichever monorepo branch the team designates.\n\n**Step 5: Verify deployment**\n\nAfter connecting, push a trivial change to `docs/content/` and verify:\n- Vercel detects the change\n- `bun install` succeeds (workspace dependencies resolve)\n- `bun run build` succeeds (Next.js + Pagefind)\n- The deployed site works correctly\n- Preview deployments work on PRs\n\n### Things that don't change\n\n- `next.config.mjs` stays the same\n- `postbuild` Pagefind step stays the same\n- PostHog integration stays the same\n- Domain/DNS stays the same\n- `vercel.json` stays the same (now at `docs/vercel.json`)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Cross-repo schema flow after migration\n\n### Before migration\n\n```\nhankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n  -> writes to hankweave/schemas/                              (local, always works)\n  -> writes to ../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/ (sibling repo, works only if checked out)\n```\n\n### After migration\n\n```\nhankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n  -> writes to hankweave/schemas/                    (local, always works)\n  -> writes to hankweave/docs/public/schemas/        (same repo, always works)\n```\n\nThe `docsAvailable` check (`fs.existsSync(path.dirname(DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR))`) becomes permanently true. The check is kept for defensive safety.\n\n### Release flow for schemas\n\n1. Developer runs `bun run generate-schemas` (or it runs as part of `bun run build`, which calls `generate-schemas` first).\n2. Schemas are written to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n3. Both locations are committed together.\n4. When the runtime is synced to public, `schemas/` goes with it; `docs/` is stripped.\n5. When docs deploy to Vercel, `docs/public/schemas/` goes with it.\n6. Both consumers always have the latest schemas -- no cross-repo coordination needed.\n\nThis is the primary concrete benefit of the monorepo: what was a fragile cross-repo file write that only worked when both repos happened to be checked out side-by-side is now a simple intra-repo operation.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Old `hankweave-docs` repo archival\n\nAfter the monorepo migration is verified and Vercel is confirmed working from the monorepo:\n\n1. Archive `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` on GitHub (read-only).\n2. Update its README to: \"This repository has been merged into SouthBridgeAI/hankweave. All future development happens there.\"\n3. Disconnect Vercel from the old repo.\n4. The old repo's git history remains accessible for reference.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Discarded files from docs repo\n\nThe `hankweave-docs/` outer wrapper contains:\n- `README.md` -- docs repo internal README. Can optionally be kept as `docs/README.md`.\n- `notes/` -- historical planning/development notes. Discard, or archive in `intermediates/docs-migration-legacy/`.\n- `plan/` -- historical planning documents. Same treatment as `notes/`.\n- `.gitignore` -- most entries are already covered by the root `.gitignore`. The `_pagefind/` entry needs to be added to root.\n\nRecommendation: Discard `notes/` and `plan/`. They are development artifacts from the docs site setup phase and have no ongoing utility.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10724,"cache_read_input_tokens":100834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10724},"output_tokens":2932,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"ca990cd7-ab1b-4693-958c-91813834c13e","timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:36:48.096Z"}
