diagrams, screenshots\n│   └── schemas/                    JSON schemas (generated by runtime's generate-schemas.ts)\n├── styles/                         Global CSS\n├── mdx-components.tsx              MDX component overrides\n├── next-env.d.ts                   Next.js TypeScript declarations\n├── next.config.mjs                 Nextra + Next.js config\n├── package.json                    hankweave-docs v2.0.0\n├── tsconfig.json                   ES2020, bundler moduleResolution, strict: false\n└── vercel.json                     Framework: nextjs, bun install/build\n```\n\nImportant: The docs use Nextra 4 with App Router conventions. Content lives in `content/` (not `pages/`), and routes are defined via the catch-all `app/[[...mdxPath]]/page.tsx` pattern.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key observations from the docs source\n\n1. **No runtime imports.** The docs site does not import TypeScript modules from `@southbridgeai/hankweave`. It references hankweave as a CLI tool (`npx hankweave`, `bunx hankweave`) but doesn't use it as a library dependency. This means no `workspace:*` dependency is needed.\n\n2. **Schema hosting.** The `public/schemas/` directory hosts JSON schemas generated by the runtime's `generate-schemas.ts`. These are served as static files referenced from docs pages. This is the only data flow from runtime to docs.\n\n3. **Layout links to public repo.** `app/layout.tsx` links to `https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` as the project URL. This doesn't change -- the public mirror continues to be the user-facing repo.\n\n4. **PostHog analytics.** Client-side integration in `app/posthog-provider.tsx`. No migration impact.\n\n5. **Pagefind search.** The `postbuild` script runs `pagefind --site .next/server/app --output-path public/_pagefind`. This runs relative to the docs workspace directory and works in the monorepo. The generated `public/_pagefind/` directory needs to be in `.gitignore`.\n\n6. **TypeScript configs are incompatible.** Runtime: `target: ES2022`, `module: ES2022`, `moduleResolution: node`, `strict: true`, types: `bun-types`. Docs: `target: ES2020`, `module: esnext`, `moduleResolution: bundler`, `strict: false`, plugins: `next`. These configs must remain separate. Do not create a shared `tsconfig.base.json`.\n\n7. **Build environment variable.** The `vercel.json` contains `\"DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969\": \"1\"` in build env. This is specific to the Vercel build and stays in `docs/vercel.json` unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SOP updates needed\n\n### 3.1: Repository structure (Section 1, lines 10-27)\n\nReplace the directory tree with the version shown in Phase 5 of the plan. Add the note about docs being a workspace that deploys to Vercel.\n\n### 3.2: Strip list documentation (Section 1, lines 31-40)\n\nAdd `docs/` to the directories list. Add a note: \"The `package.json` transformation also removes the `\\\"workspaces\\\"` field to prevent the public repo from referencing the missing docs directory.\"\n\n### 3.3: Key files reference (Section 9, lines 337-354)\n\nAdd:\n```\n| `docs/package.json`         | Documentation site workspace (hankweave-docs)              |\n| `docs/content/`             | MDX documentation pages (concepts, guides, reference)      |\n```\n\n### 3.4: Development workflow (Section 3)\n\nAdd a \"Documentation site\" subsection describing how to run `bun run dev` and `bun run build` from `docs/`, and how `bun run generate-schemas` writes to both schema locations.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Documentation that should NOT be updated\n\n### User-facing docs (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`)\n\nThe docs cover concepts, guides, and reference material for hankweave users. None reference the repository structure. The monorepo migration is invisible to users.\n\n### Public README (`public-release-files/README.md`)\n\nDescribes the public mirror repo. The monorepo structure is not visible to public users.\n\n### CHANGELOG\n\nOptional -- can add an internal note under `[Unreleased] > Changed` but it's not user-facing.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Vercel deployment migration\n\n### Current state\n\nThe docs deploy from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs`. Vercel runs:\n1. `bun install` (as specified in `vercel.json`)\n2. `bun run build` (Next.js build + Pagefind postbuild)\n3. Deploy the `.next` output\n\n### Required changes\n\n**Step 1: Connect Vercel to the monorepo**\n1. Go to the Vercel project settings for hankweave-docs.\n2. Under \"Git\" -> \"Connected Git Repository\", change from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`.\n3. Set \"Root Directory\" to `docs`.\n4. Verify Framework Preset is \"Next.js\".\n\n**Step 2: Validate install behavior**\n\nWhen Vercel sets root to `docs/` and runs `bun install` there, Bun should detect it's a workspace member and look upward for the root `package.json`. If this works correctly, the full workspace dependency tree is installed using the root `bun.lock`.\n\nIf this fails (Vercel only mounts the subdirectory and Bun can't find the workspace root):\n- Set Vercel root directory to `/` (repo root)\n- Set install command to `bun install`\n- Set build command to `cd docs && bun run build`\n- Vercel will detect Next.js from the `docs/` directory\n\n**Step 3: Configure \"Ignored Build Step\" (recommended)**\n1. Go to Settings -> General -> \"Ignored Build Step\".\n2. Set to: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n\nThis prevents unnecessary rebuilds when only runtime code changes.\n\n**Step 4: Configure branch deployment**\n\nThe monorepo uses `develop` and `release/alpha` branches. Configure Vercel production and preview deployment branches according to team preference. Currently the docs repo likely deploys from `main` -- this changes to whichever monorepo branch the team designates.\n\n**Step 5: Verify deployment**\n\nAfter connecting, push a trivial change to `docs/content/` and verify:\n- Vercel detects the change\n- `bun install` succeeds (workspace dependencies resolve)\n- `bun run build` succeeds (Next.js + Pagefind)\n- The deployed site works correctly\n- Preview deployments work on PRs\n\n### Things that don't change\n\n- `next.config.mjs` stays the same\n- `postbuild` Pagefind step stays the same\n- PostHog integration stays the same\n- Domain/DNS stays the same\n- `vercel.json` stays the same (now at `docs/vercel.json`)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Cross-repo schema flow after migration\n\n### Before migration\n\n```\nhankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n  -> writes to hankweave/schemas/                              (local, always works)\n  -> writes to ../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/ (sibling repo, works only if checked out)\n```\n\n### After migration\n\n```\nhankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n  -> writes to hankweave/schemas/                    (local, always works)\n  -> writes to hankweave/docs/public/schemas/        (same repo, always works)\n```\n\nThe `docsAvailable` check (`fs.existsSync(path.dirname(DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR))`) becomes permanently true. The check is kept for defensive safety.\n\n### Release flow for schemas\n\n1. Developer runs `bun run generate-schemas` (or it runs as part of `bun run build`, which calls `generate-schemas` first).\n2. Schemas are written to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n3. Both locations are committed together.\n4. When the runtime is synced to public, `schemas/` goes with it; `docs/` is stripped.\n5. When docs deploy to Vercel, `docs/public/schemas/` goes with it.\n6. Both consumers always have the latest schemas -- no cross-repo coordination needed.\n\nThis is the primary concrete benefit of the monorepo: what was a fragile cross-repo file write that only worked when both repos happened to be checked out side-by-side is now a simple intra-repo operation.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Old `hankweave-docs` repo archival\n\nAfter the monorepo migration is verified and Vercel is confirmed working from the monorepo:\n\n1. Archive `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` on GitHub (read-only).\n2. Update its README to: \"This repository has been merged into SouthBridgeAI/hankweave. All future development happens there.\"\n3. Disconnect Vercel from the old repo.\n4. The old repo's git history remains accessible for reference.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Discarded files from docs repo\n\nThe `hankweave-docs/` outer wrapper contains:\n- `README.md` -- docs repo internal README. Can optionally be kept as `docs/README.md`.\n- `notes/` -- historical planning/development notes. Discard, or archive in `intermediates/docs-migration-legacy/`.\n- `plan/` -- historical planning documents. Same treatment as `notes/`.\n- `.gitignore` -- most entries are already covered by the root `.gitignore`. The `_pagefind/` entry needs to be added to root.\n\nRecommendation: Discard `notes/` and `plan/`. They are development artifacts from the docs site setup phase and have no ongoing utility.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:36:48.515Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QogoXuFNgyezFuDa8dJabk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PWnZLvtS5zeHFGxAi1uePs","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md","content":"# Addendum: Testing and CI/CD Considerations\n\nRead alongside `plan.md`. Covers test impact analysis, CI/CD adjustments, and verification procedures for the monorepo migration.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Test infrastructure overview\n\nThe test suite is organized in four tiers, all living under `tests/`:\n\n| Tier | Location | Runner | Count | External deps | Migration impact |\n|------|----------|--------|-------|--------------|-----------------|\n| Unit | `tests/unit/` | `bun:test` | 65+ files | None | None |\n| Integration | `tests/integration/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Mock LLM | None |\n| E2E | `tests/e2e/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Real API keys | None |\n| Cross-runtime | `tests/cross-runtime/` | bun/node/deno | 3+ files | None | None |\n\nAll tests import from `../../server/<module>` using relative paths from within `tests/`. Since `server/` is not moving, no test imports change.\n\n### Test runner configuration\n\n- `bunfig.toml` sets `BUN_TEST=1` environment variable.\n- `package.json` defines test scripts: `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `test`, `test:e2e:init`, `test:cross-runtime:*`.\n- CI uses composite action `.github/actions/run-tests/action.yml` which calls `bun test tests/unit` and `bun test tests/integration`.\n\n### Test utilities\n\nKey utilities at `tests/utils/`:\n- `sentinel-test-harness.ts` -- mock LLM calls, event tracking, test workspace management\n- `mock-llm.ts` -- typed mock LLM provider with configurable responses\n- `env-test-helpers.ts` -- environment variable capture/restore for test isolation\n\nNone of these reference paths outside the runtime package.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Existing tests affected\n\n### Directly affected: None\n\nNo existing test file needs modification. The migration changes:\n1. Root `package.json` (adds `\"workspaces\"` field)\n2. Scripts in `scripts/` (path adjustments, strip list updates)\n3. `.gitignore` (docs artifacts)\n4. SOP document\n\nNone of these are read by tests.\n\n### Individually verified (low risk, no changes needed)\n\n1. **`tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts`** -- Tests that generated schemas validate correctly. Reads from `schemas/` which is unchanged. The migration only affects where schemas are *also* written (now `docs/public/schemas/` instead of a sibling repo path).\n\n2. **`tests/integration/schema-zod-parity.test.ts`** -- Verifies Zod schemas match JSON schemas. Reads from `schemas/`, not affected.\n\n3. **`tests/unit/utils.test.ts`** -- Uses `getMetadata()` which extracts `name` and `version` from `package.json`. The `\"workspaces\"` field addition doesn't interfere with `name` or `version` parsing.\n\n4. **E2E init tests** -- Test the `--init` scaffolding flow. The runtime code is unchanged.\n\n5. **Cross-runtime tests** -- `run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. Path doesn't change.\n\n---\n\n## 3. New tests\n\n### Strictly required: None\n\nThe migration is structural (directory layout, workspace configuration), not behavioral. Runtime behavior is identical before and after.\n\n### Optional monorepo smoke test\n\nA lightweight structural invariant test:\n\n```typescript\n// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\nimport { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\n\ndescribe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n\n  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs schemas directory exists\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nOnly add if the team wants structural tests. This follows the existing test conventions: `bun:test` framework, relative imports, `tests/unit/` location.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Edge cases\n\n### 4.1: `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI\n\nAfter migration, CI runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` (at `.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml:34`). The new unified `bun.lock` must be committed as part of the migration PR. If it's missing or stale, CI will fail because `--frozen-lockfile` disallows lockfile generation.\n\nThe new lockfile will include the docs workspace's dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, `pagefind`, etc.) in addition to all existing runtime dependencies. This is a normal and expected change.\n\n### 4.2: Dependency hoisting\n\nBun workspaces hoists dependencies to the root `node_modules/`. The runtime and docs have almost entirely different dependency trees:\n- Runtime: `@ai-sdk/*`, `zod`, `srvx`, `crossws`, `simple-git`, etc.\n- Docs: `next`, `nextra`, `react`, `react-dom`, `posthog-js`, `@vercel/analytics`\n\nThe only shared dependency is `typescript` (runtime: `^5.9.2` as peer dep; docs: `^5.0.0` as dev dep). Bun will hoist a single version that satisfies both ranges. No conflicts expected.\n\n### 4.3: npm publish from root\n\nThe `release.yml` workflow runs `npm publish` from repo root. The `\"files\"` field in `package.json`:\n```json\n\"files\": [\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]\n```\n\nThis is an allowlist -- only listed paths are included in the npm tarball. `docs/` will not be published. The `.npmignore` is irrelevant because `\"files\"` takes precedence.\n\nVerify with: `npm pack --dry-run` (Phase 6, Step 6.5 of the plan).\n\n### 4.4: Build executable\n\n`build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and resolves paths from `import.meta.dir`. These paths don't change with workspace addition. The build should produce identical output.\n\n### 4.5: Cross-platform path separators\n\nThe CI matrix includes Ubuntu, Windows, and macOS. Bun handles path separators internally for workspace resolution. Workspace paths in `package.json` use forward slashes (`\"docs\"`) which work on all platforms. No issues expected, but the first CI run after migration should be monitored on all three OS variants.\n\n### 4.6: Lockfile churn\n\nThe unified `bun.lock` covers both workspaces. Docs dependency updates (e.g., `next` minor bump) will modify the lockfile even when no runtime code is affected. This is normal for monorepos and a minor inconvenience. It does not affect runtime behavior.\n\n### 4.7: CI time increase\n\nCI now installs docs dependencies even when only runtime code changed. This adds approximately 10-20 seconds to `bun install` (docs dependencies are mostly React/Next.js which are not large). Not worth optimizing initially. If it becomes a concern, `paths:` filtering in CI workflow triggers can skip docs-irrelevant jobs.\n\n---\n\n## 5. CI/CD adjustments\n\n### Required changes: None\n\nAll existing CI workflows work without modification if the runtime stays at root:\n- **ci.yml**: Checks out code, runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, runs lint/typecheck/tests. All of these operate on the runtime which hasn't moved. `bun install` now also installs docs deps (harmless). Tests run from `tests/unit` and `tests/integration` which are unchanged.\n- **release.yml**: Triggered by `v*` tags. Runs `npm publish` from root, builds binaries, creates GitHub release. All paths are runtime-relative and unchanged.\n- **sync-public.yml**: Manually triggered. Checks out at tag into `private/`, runs `bun private/scripts/sync-public.ts`. The script's strip lists (updated in Phase 3) handle the new `docs/` directory.\n\n### Recommended optional additions\n\n**1. Docs build CI job**\n\nAdd a `docs-build` job to `ci.yml` to catch docs breakage from monorepo-level changes:\n\n```yaml\ndocs-build:\n  name: Docs Build Check\n  runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n  timeout-minutes: 10\n  steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Setup environment\n      uses: ./.github/actions/setup-environment\n      with:\n        install-gemini: \"false\"\n        codex-auth-json: \"\"\n    - name: Build docs\n      run: cd docs && bun run build\n```\n\nThis catches scenarios where a lockfile update, dependency resolution change, or workspace configuration issue breaks the docs build. Without it, broken docs would only be caught by Vercel deployment failures.\n\n**2. Schema generation check (optional)**\n\nA CI step that runs `bun run generate-schemas` and verifies no uncommitted changes:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Verify schemas are up to date\n  run: |\n    bun run generate-schemas\n    git diff --exit-code schemas/ docs/public/schemas/\n```\n\nThis ensures schema generation stays in sync. If schemas are always regenerated before commit (via `bun run build` which calls `generate-schemas` first), this is redundant. Add only if schema drift has been a historical problem.\n\n**3. Path filtering (future)**\n\nIf CI time becomes a concern, add `paths:` filters to CI triggers:\n\n```yaml\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [develop, release/alpha]\n    paths-ignore:\n      - 'docs/**'\n      - '*.md'\n```\n\nThis skips the full runtime test matrix on docs-only changes. Not recommended initially -- for two packages, running everything is simpler and fast enough.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Verification checklist\n\nAfter migration, run these checks to confirm everything works:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Workspace installs correctly\nbun install\n# Expected: success, single bun.lock at root\n\n# 2. Runtime tests still pass\nbun run test:unit\nbun run test:integration\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\n\n# 3. Schema generation writes to both locations\nbun run generate-schemas\nls schemas/hank.schema.json          # runtime schemas\nls docs/public/schemas/hank.schema.json  # docs schemas\n\n# 4. Runtime build works\nbun run build\nls dist/index.js\n\n# 5. Docs build works\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n# Verify: .next/ directory created, public/_pagefind/ generated by postbuild\n\n# 6. npm pack excludes docs\nnpm pack --dry-run\n# Expected: docs/ NOT in the file list\n\n# 7. Sync dry-run strips docs correctly\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <version> --use-head\n# Expected: \"Correctly removed: docs\" in verification output\n# Expected: public package.json has no \"workspaces\" field\n\n# 8. Release dry-run validates (if on develop with clean tree)\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n# Expected: all validations pass\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Risks\n\n1. **Lockfile convergence is the main operational risk.** CI fails early and loudly if the lockfile is wrong, so the risk is low-consequence (easily fixed by regenerating). But it's the most likely source of first-run issues.\n\n2. **Vercel install behavior.** If Vercel can't resolve workspace dependencies from the `docs/` subdirectory, the fallback (set root to `/` with `cd docs && bun run build`) is straightforward. See the docs addendum for details.\n\n3. **No runtime code changes.** The migration doesn't touch any file under `server/`, `types/`, `shims/`, or `schemas/`. Runtime behavior is identical. If any test fails after migration, it's a workspace configuration issue (likely lockfile-related), not a code regression.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2986,"cache_read_input_tokens":111558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2986},"output_tokens":3179,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"980fcc74-8d4f-4706-8e29-cd2776cdae73","timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:38:00.291Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PWnZLvtS5zeHFGxAi1uePs","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"86ec80af-bf45-46a3-9639-c233c7a64285","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md","content":"# Addendum: Testing and CI/CD Considerations\n\nRead alongside `plan.md`. Covers test impact analysis, CI/CD adjustments, and verification procedures for the monorepo migration.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Test infrastructure overview\n\nThe test suite is organized in four tiers, all living under `tests/`:\n\n| Tier | Location | Runner | Count | External deps | Migration impact |\n|------|----------|--------|-------|--------------|-----------------|\n| Unit | `tests/unit/` | `bun:test` | 65+ files | None | None |\n| Integration | `tests/integration/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Mock LLM | None |\n| E2E | `tests/e2e/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Real API keys | None |\n| Cross-runtime | `tests/cross-runtime/` | bun/node/deno | 3+ files | None | None |\n\nAll tests import from `../../server/<module>` using relative paths from within `tests/`. Since `server/` is not moving, no test imports change.\n\n### Test runner configuration\n\n- `bunfig.toml` sets `BUN_TEST=1` environment variable.\n- `package.json` defines test scripts: `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `test`, `test:e2e:init`, `test:cross-runtime:*`.\n- CI uses composite action `.github/actions/run-tests/action.yml` which calls `bun test tests/unit` and `bun test tests/integration`.\n\n### Test utilities\n\nKey utilities at `tests/utils/`:\n- `sentinel-test-harness.ts` -- mock LLM calls, event tracking, test workspace management\n- `mock-llm.ts` -- typed mock LLM provider with configurable responses\n- `env-test-helpers.ts` -- environment variable capture/restore for test isolation\n\nNone of these reference paths outside the runtime package.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Existing tests affected\n\n### Directly affected: None\n\nNo existing test file needs modification. The migration changes:\n1. Root `package.json` (adds `\"workspaces\"` field)\n2. Scripts in `scripts/` (path adjustments, strip list updates)\n3. `.gitignore` (docs artifacts)\n4. SOP document\n\nNone of these are read by tests.\n\n### Individually verified (low risk, no changes needed)\n\n1. **`tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts`** -- Tests that generated schemas validate correctly. Reads from `schemas/` which is unchanged. The migration only affects where schemas are *also* written (now `docs/public/schemas/` instead of a sibling repo path).\n\n2. **`tests/integration/schema-zod-parity.test.ts`** -- Verifies Zod schemas match JSON schemas. Reads from `schemas/`, not affected.\n\n3. **`tests/unit/utils.test.ts`** -- Uses `getMetadata()` which extracts `name` and `version` from `package.json`. The `\"workspaces\"` field addition doesn't interfere with `name` or `version` parsing.\n\n4. **E2E init tests** -- Test the `--init` scaffolding flow. The runtime code is unchanged.\n\n5. **Cross-runtime tests** -- `run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. Path doesn't change.\n\n---\n\n## 3. New tests\n\n### Strictly required: None\n\nThe migration is structural (directory layout, workspace configuration), not behavioral. Runtime behavior is identical before and after.\n\n### Optional monorepo smoke test\n\nA lightweight structural invariant test:\n\n```typescript\n// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\nimport { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\n\ndescribe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n\n  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs schemas directory exists\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nOnly add if the team wants structural tests. This follows the existing test conventions: `bun:test` framework, relative imports, `tests/unit/` location.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Edge cases\n\n### 4.1: `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI\n\nAfter migration, CI runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` (at `.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml:34`). The new unified `bun.lock` must be committed as part of the migration PR. If it's missing or stale, CI will fail because `--frozen-lockfile` disallows lockfile generation.\n\nThe new lockfile will include the docs workspace's dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, `pagefind`, etc.) in addition to all existing runtime dependencies. This is a normal and expected change.\n\n### 4.2: Dependency hoisting\n\nBun workspaces hoists dependencies to the root `node_modules/`. The runtime and docs have almost entirely different dependency trees:\n- Runtime: `@ai-sdk/*`, `zod`, `srvx`, `crossws`, `simple-git`, etc.\n- Docs: `next`, `nextra`, `react`, `react-dom`, `posthog-js`, `@vercel/analytics`\n\nThe only shared dependency is `typescript` (runtime: `^5.9.2` as peer dep; docs: `^5.0.0` as dev dep). Bun will hoist a single version that satisfies both ranges. No conflicts expected.\n\n### 4.3: npm publish from root\n\nThe `release.yml` workflow runs `npm publish` from repo root. The `\"files\"` field in `package.json`:\n```json\n\"files\": [\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]\n```\n\nThis is an allowlist -- only listed paths are included in the npm tarball. `docs/` will not be published. The `.npmignore` is irrelevant because `\"files\"` takes precedence.\n\nVerify with: `npm pack --dry-run` (Phase 6, Step 6.5 of the plan).\n\n### 4.4: Build executable\n\n`build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and resolves paths from `import.meta.dir`. These paths don't change with workspace addition. The build should produce identical output.\n\n### 4.5: Cross-platform path separators\n\nThe CI matrix includes Ubuntu, Windows, and macOS. Bun handles path separators internally for workspace resolution. Workspace paths in `package.json` use forward slashes (`\"docs\"`) which work on all platforms. No issues expected, but the first CI run after migration should be monitored on all three OS variants.\n\n### 4.6: Lockfile churn\n\nThe unified `bun.lock` covers both workspaces. Docs dependency updates (e.g., `next` minor bump) will modify the lockfile even when no runtime code is affected. This is normal for monorepos and a minor inconvenience. It does not affect runtime behavior.\n\n### 4.7: CI time increase\n\nCI now installs docs dependencies even when only runtime code changed. This adds approximately 10-20 seconds to `bun install` (docs dependencies are mostly React/Next.js which are not large). Not worth optimizing initially. If it becomes a concern, `paths:` filtering in CI workflow triggers can skip docs-irrelevant jobs.\n\n---\n\n## 5. CI/CD adjustments\n\n### Required changes: None\n\nAll existing CI workflows work without modification if the runtime stays at root:\n- **ci.yml**: Checks out code, runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, runs lint/typecheck/tests. All of these operate on the runtime which hasn't moved. `bun install` now also installs docs deps (harmless). Tests run from `tests/unit` and `tests/integration` which are unchanged.\n- **release.yml**: Triggered by `v*` tags. Runs `npm publish` from root, builds binaries, creates GitHub release. All paths are runtime-relative and unchanged.\n- **sync-public.yml**: Manually triggered. Checks out at tag into `private/`, runs `bun private/scripts/sync-public.ts`. The script's strip lists (updated in Phase 3) handle the new `docs/` directory.\n\n### Recommended optional additions\n\n**1. Docs build CI job**\n\nAdd a `docs-build` job to `ci.yml` to catch docs breakage from monorepo-level changes:\n\n```yaml\ndocs-build:\n  name: Docs Build Check\n  runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n  timeout-minutes: 10\n  steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Setup environment\n      uses: ./.github/actions/setup-environment\n      with:\n        install-gemini: \"false\"\n        codex-auth-json: \"\"\n    - name: Build docs\n      run: cd docs && bun run build\n```\n\nThis catches scenarios where a lockfile update, dependency resolution change, or workspace configuration issue breaks the docs build. Without it, broken docs would only be caught by Vercel deployment failures.\n\n**2. Schema generation check (optional)**\n\nA CI step that runs `bun run generate-schemas` and verifies no uncommitted changes:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Verify schemas are up to date\n  run: |\n    bun run generate-schemas\n    git diff --exit-code schemas/ docs/public/schemas/\n```\n\nThis ensures schema generation stays in sync. If schemas are always regenerated before commit (via `bun run build` which calls `generate-schemas` first), this is redundant. Add only if schema drift has been a historical problem.\n\n**3. Path filtering (future)**\n\nIf CI time becomes a concern, add `paths:` filters to CI triggers:\n\n```yaml\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [develop, release/alpha]\n    paths-ignore:\n      - 'docs/**'\n      - '*.md'\n```\n\nThis skips the full runtime test matrix on docs-only changes. Not recommended initially -- for two packages, running everything is simpler and fast enough.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Verification checklist\n\nAfter migration, run these checks to confirm everything works:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Workspace installs correctly\nbun install\n# Expected: success, single bun.lock at root\n\n# 2. Runtime tests still pass\nbun run test:unit\nbun run test:integration\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\n\n# 3. Schema generation writes to both locations\nbun run generate-schemas\nls schemas/hank.schema.json          # runtime schemas\nls docs/public/schemas/hank.schema.json  # docs schemas\n\n# 4. Runtime build works\nbun run build\nls dist/index.js\n\n# 5. Docs build works\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n# Verify: .next/ directory created, public/_pagefind/ generated by postbuild\n\n# 6. npm pack excludes docs\nnpm pack --dry-run\n# Expected: docs/ NOT in the file list\n\n# 7. Sync dry-run strips docs correctly\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <version> --use-head\n# Expected: \"Correctly removed: docs\" in verification output\n# Expected: public package.json has no \"workspaces\" field\n\n# 8. Release dry-run validates (if on develop with clean tree)\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n# Expected: all validations pass\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Risks\n\n1. **Lockfile convergence is the main operational risk.** CI fails early and loudly if the lockfile is wrong, so the risk is low-consequence (easily fixed by regenerating). But it's the most likely source of first-run issues.\n\n2. **Vercel install behavior.** If Vercel can't resolve workspace dependencies from the `docs/` subdirectory, the fallback (set root to `/` with `cd docs && bun run build`) is straightforward. See the docs addendum for details.\n\n3. **No runtime code changes.** The migration doesn't touch any file under `server/`, `types/`, `shims/`, or `schemas/`. Runtime behavior is identical. If any test fails after migration, it's a workspace configuration issue (likely lockfile-related), not a code regression.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:38:00.689Z"}
