{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JwjEAu1hzPSXZwhPjHfkmc","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Plan: Migrate Hankweave to Monorepo\n     2→\n     3→## a. The Main Task\n     4→\n     5→Consolidate the `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` (runtime) and `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` (documentation site) repositories into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime package stays at the repository root. The docs site moves in as a workspace at `docs/`, flattened from its current `nextra-site/` subdirectory. The existing CI/CD pipelines, release process, public sync workflow, and Vercel docs deployment continue to function with targeted, minimal changes.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## b. Information Available\n    10→\n    11→### Sources that informed this plan\n    12→\n    13→1. **Task specification** -- `plan/task.md` (task description, open questions, research on Bun workspaces, Turborepo, and git subtree merges).\n    14→2. **Opus plan and addendums** -- `plan/rough-workspace/opus/plan.md`, `addendum-docs.md`, `addendum-tests.md`, `log.md`. Detailed, phase-by-phase plan with exact file diffs, SOP drafts, and edge case analysis.\n    15→3. **Codex plan and addendums** -- `plan/rough-workspace/codex/plan.md`, `addendum-1.md` (tests/CI), `addendum-2.md` (docs/deployment). Shorter plan with a notable catch on the `transformPackageJson()` gap for stripping `\"workspaces\"` from the public `package.json`.\n    16→4. **Full source code review** -- Every config, script, workflow, and representative server/test file from both `source/hankweave/` and `source/hankweave-docs/`.\n    17→\n    18→### What I could see\n    19→\n    20→- Full directory structure and file contents of both repos.\n    21→- All CI workflows (ci.yml, release.yml, sync-public.yml), composite actions (setup-environment, run-tests, dump-test-logs), and scripts (build.ts, build-executable.ts, release.ts, sync-public.ts, generate-schemas.ts, test-sync-local.ts, e2e/init.ts, run-cross-runtime-tests.ts).\n    22→- Both `package.json` files, both `tsconfig.json` files, `biome.json`, `bunfig.toml`.\n    23→- The full docs Nextra/Next.js setup including `vercel.json`, `next.config.mjs`, `app/`, `content/`, `components/`, `public/`, `styles/`.\n    24→- The SOP document (`standard-operating-procedures.md`).\n    25→- The `.gitignore` files from both repos.\n    26→\n    27→### What I could NOT see\n    28→\n    29→- The actual GitHub repos (branch protection rules, secrets, default branches, collaborator list).\n    30→- The Vercel project dashboard settings (current root directory config, branch deployment rules).\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"ff61d633-4fa0-4d68-b878-e3e254874737","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Migrate Hankweave to Monorepo\n\n## a. The Main Task\n\nConsolidate the `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` (runtime) and `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` (documentation site) repositories into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime package stays at the repository root. The docs site moves in as a workspace at `docs/`, flattened from its current `nextra-site/` subdirectory. The existing CI/CD pipelines, release process, public sync workflow, and Vercel docs deployment continue to function with targeted, minimal changes.\n\n---\n\n## b. Information Available\n\n### Sources that informed this plan\n\n1. **Task specification** -- `plan/task.md` (task description, open questions, research on Bun workspaces, Turborepo, and git subtree merges).\n2. **Opus plan and addendums** -- `plan/rough-workspace/opus/plan.md`, `addendum-docs.md`, `addendum-tests.md`, `log.md`. Detailed, phase-by-phase plan with exact file diffs, SOP drafts, and edge case analysis.\n3. **Codex plan and addendums** -- `plan/rough-workspace/codex/plan.md`, `addendum-1.md` (tests/CI), `addendum-2.md` (docs/deployment). Shorter plan with a notable catch on the `transformPackageJson()` gap for stripping `\"workspaces\"` from the public `package.json`.\n4. **Full source code review** -- Every config, script, workflow, and representative server/test file from both `source/hankweave/` and `source/hankweave-docs/`.\n\n### What I could see\n\n- Full directory structure and file contents of both repos.\n- All CI workflows (ci.yml, release.yml, sync-public.yml), composite actions (setup-environment, run-tests, dump-test-logs), and scripts (build.ts, build-executable.ts, release.ts, sync-public.ts, generate-schemas.ts, test-sync-local.ts, e2e/init.ts, run-cross-runtime-tests.ts).\n- Both `package.json` files, both `tsconfig.json` files, `biome.json`, `bunfig.toml`.\n- The full docs Nextra/Next.js setup including `vercel.json`, `next.config.mjs`, `app/`, `content/`, `components/`, `public/`, `styles/`.\n- The SOP document (`standard-operating-procedures.md`).\n- The `.gitignore` files from both repos.\n\n### What I could NOT see\n\n- The actual GitHub repos (branch protection rules, secrets, default branches, collaborator list).\n- The Vercel project dashboard settings (current root directory config, branch deployment rules).","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":758}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:38:41.407Z"}
