{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XZZXcPQ3eb1nNhyHBfkv8T","type":"tool_result","content":"   345→  // 7. Test merge feasibility\n   346→  logStep(\"Testing merge feasibility (develop → release/alpha)...\");\n   347→  try {\n   348→    // Use merge-tree to check for conflicts without touching the working tree\n   349→    // merge-tree returns 0 even with conflicts, but outputs conflict markers\n   350→    // Instead, do a merge --no-commit --no-ff and then abort\n   351→    await exec(\"git checkout release/alpha\", { silent: true });\n   352→    const mergeResult = await exec(\n   353→      \"git merge --no-commit --no-ff develop 2>&1\",\n   354→      {\n   355→        silent: true,\n   356→        allowFailure: true,\n   357→      },\n   358→    );\n   359→    // Check for conflicts — any unmerged entry in porcelain status.\n   360→    // Codes: UU (both modified), AA (both added), DD (both deleted),\n   361→    // DU/UD (modify/delete — e.g. file stripped on release but modified on develop)\n   362→    const mergeStatus = await exec(\"git status --porcelain\", { silent: true });\n   363→    const conflictPattern = /^(UU|AA|DD|DU|UD|AU|UA) /m;\n   364→    const hasConflicts = conflictPattern.test(mergeStatus);\n   365→\n   366→    // For modify/delete conflicts, check if ALL conflicting files are in the\n   367→    // strip list — if so, the merge step will auto-resolve them.\n   368→    let conflictsAreStrippable = false;\n   369→    if (hasConflicts) {\n   370→      const modifyDeletePattern = /^(DU|UD) (.+)$/gm;\n   371→      const allConflictPattern = /^(UU|AA|DD|DU|UD|AU|UA) (.+)$/gm;\n   372→\n   373→      const modifyDeleteFiles = [...mergeStatus.matchAll(modifyDeletePattern)].map((m) => m[2].trim());\n   374→      const allConflictFiles = [...mergeStatus.matchAll(allConflictPattern)].map((m) => m[2].trim());\n   375→\n   376→      if (\n   377→        allConflictFiles.length > 0 &&\n   378→        allConflictFiles.length === modifyDeleteFiles.length &&\n   379→        modifyDeleteFiles.every((f) =>\n   380→          INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP.some((s) => f === s || f.startsWith(s)),\n   381→        )\n   382→      ) {\n   383→        conflictsAreStrippable = true;\n   384→      }\n   385→    }\n   386→\n   387→    // Abort the merge\n   388→    await exec(\"git merge --abort 2>/dev/null || git reset --hard HEAD\", {\n   389→      silent: true,\n   390→      allowFailure: true,\n   391→    });\n   392→    await exec(\"git checkout develop\", { silent: true });\n   393→\n   394→    if (hasConflicts && !conflictsAreStrippable) {\n   395→      logErr(\"Merge would have conflicts. Resolve before releasing:\");\n   396→      logErr(\"  git checkout release/alpha\");\n   397→      logErr(\"  git merge develop\");\n   398→      logErr(\"  # resolve conflicts, commit, then:\");\n   399→      logErr(\"  git checkout develop\");\n   400→      process.exit(1);\n   401→    }\n   402→    result.mergeWouldSucceed = true;\n   403→    if (conflictsAreStrippable) {\n   404→      logOk(\"Merge has modify/delete conflicts on stripped files (will auto-resolve)\");\n   405→    } else {\n   406→      logOk(\"Merge would succeed cleanly\");\n   407→    }\n   408→  } catch (error) {\n   409→    // Make sure we're back on develop\n   410→    await exec(\"git merge --abort 2>/dev/null || true\", {\n   411→      silent: true,\n   412→      allowFailure: true,\n   413→    });\n   414→    await exec(\"git checkout develop 2>/dev/null || true\", {\n   415→      silent: true,\n   416→      allowFailure: true,\n   417→    });\n   418→    logErr(`Merge test failed: ${(error as Error).message}`);\n   419→    process.exit(1);\n   420→  }\n   421→\n   422→  // 8. Test schema generation\n   423→  logStep(\"Testing schema generation...\");\n   424→  try {\n   425→    await exec(\"bun run generate-schemas\", { silent: true });\n   426→    // Check if schemas directory changed (would indicate schemas need regenerating)\n   427→    const schemaChanges = await exec(\"git diff --name-only schemas/\", {\n   428→      silent: true,\n   429→    });\n   430→    if (schemaChanges) {\n   431→      logWarn(\n   432→        \"Schema generation produced changes (will be included in release commit)\",\n   433→      );\n   434→    }\n   435→    // Reset any changes from test generation\n   436→    await exec(\"git checkout -- schemas/ 2>/dev/null || true\", {\n   437→      silent: true,\n   438→      allowFailure: true,\n   439→    });\n   440→    result.schemasWouldGenerate = true;\n   441→    logOk(\"Schema generation works\");\n   442→  } catch {\n   443→    logErr(\"Schema generation failed. Fix before releasing.\");\n   444→    process.exit(1);\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"6568e7fc-699a-448b-a7a4-44bc94f48945","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/scripts/release.ts","content":"  // 7. Test merge feasibility\n  logStep(\"Testing merge feasibility (develop → release/alpha)...\");\n  try {\n    // Use merge-tree to check for conflicts without touching the working tree\n    // merge-tree returns 0 even with conflicts, but outputs conflict markers\n    // Instead, do a merge --no-commit --no-ff and then abort\n    await exec(\"git checkout release/alpha\", { silent: true });\n    const mergeResult = await exec(\n      \"git merge --no-commit --no-ff develop 2>&1\",\n      {\n        silent: true,\n        allowFailure: true,\n      },\n    );\n    // Check for conflicts — any unmerged entry in porcelain status.\n    // Codes: UU (both modified), AA (both added), DD (both deleted),\n    // DU/UD (modify/delete — e.g. file stripped on release but modified on develop)\n    const mergeStatus = await exec(\"git status --porcelain\", { silent: true });\n    const conflictPattern = /^(UU|AA|DD|DU|UD|AU|UA) /m;\n    const hasConflicts = conflictPattern.test(mergeStatus);\n\n    // For modify/delete conflicts, check if ALL conflicting files are in the\n    // strip list — if so, the merge step will auto-resolve them.\n    let conflictsAreStrippable = false;\n    if (hasConflicts) {\n      const modifyDeletePattern = /^(DU|UD) (.+)$/gm;\n      const allConflictPattern = /^(UU|AA|DD|DU|UD|AU|UA) (.+)$/gm;\n\n      const modifyDeleteFiles = [...mergeStatus.matchAll(modifyDeletePattern)].map((m) => m[2].trim());\n      const allConflictFiles = [...mergeStatus.matchAll(allConflictPattern)].map((m) => m[2].trim());\n\n      if (\n        allConflictFiles.length > 0 &&\n        allConflictFiles.length === modifyDeleteFiles.length &&\n        modifyDeleteFiles.every((f) =>\n          INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP.some((s) => f === s || f.startsWith(s)),\n        )\n      ) {\n        conflictsAreStrippable = true;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Abort the merge\n    await exec(\"git merge --abort 2>/dev/null || git reset --hard HEAD\", {\n      silent: true,\n      allowFailure: true,\n    });\n    await exec(\"git checkout develop\", { silent: true });\n\n    if (hasConflicts && !conflictsAreStrippable) {\n      logErr(\"Merge would have conflicts. Resolve before releasing:\");\n      logErr(\"  git checkout release/alpha\");\n      logErr(\"  git merge develop\");\n      logErr(\"  # resolve conflicts, commit, then:\");\n      logErr(\"  git checkout develop\");\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n    result.mergeWouldSucceed = true;\n    if (conflictsAreStrippable) {\n      logOk(\"Merge has modify/delete conflicts on stripped files (will auto-resolve)\");\n    } else {\n      logOk(\"Merge would succeed cleanly\");\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    // Make sure we're back on develop\n    await exec(\"git merge --abort 2>/dev/null || true\", {\n      silent: true,\n      allowFailure: true,\n    });\n    await exec(\"git checkout develop 2>/dev/null || true\", {\n      silent: true,\n      allowFailure: true,\n    });\n    logErr(`Merge test failed: ${(error as Error).message}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  // 8. Test schema generation\n  logStep(\"Testing schema generation...\");\n  try {\n    await exec(\"bun run generate-schemas\", { silent: true });\n    // Check if schemas directory changed (would indicate schemas need regenerating)\n    const schemaChanges = await exec(\"git diff --name-only schemas/\", {\n      silent: true,\n    });\n    if (schemaChanges) {\n      logWarn(\n        \"Schema generation produced changes (will be included in release commit)\",\n      );\n    }\n    // Reset any changes from test generation\n    await exec(\"git checkout -- schemas/ 2>/dev/null || true\", {\n      silent: true,\n      allowFailure: true,\n    });\n    result.schemasWouldGenerate = true;\n    logOk(\"Schema generation works\");\n  } catch {\n    logErr(\"Schema generation failed. Fix before releasing.\");\n    process.exit(1);","numLines":100,"startLine":345,"totalLines":868}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:38:58.100Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YXCnbNHBBpVxoMY2PdJL3H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is an important nuance. The release script has built-in logic to handle merge conflicts on files that are in the `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` list -- it treats modify/delete conflicts on stripped files as auto-resolvable. Once `docs/` is added to the strip list, any modify/delete conflicts on docs files during the `develop -> release/alpha` merge will be auto-resolved. This is exactly the right behavior and neither plan explicitly calls it out. Let me add a note about this to the plan."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1859,"cache_read_input_tokens":100373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1859},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"b96a00ad-fec7-4119-a899-fa1b2df79448","timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:39:03.617Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YXCnbNHBBpVxoMY2PdJL3H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MN6qfzqi3pY76WMH2a1GqP","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","old_string":"This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step).\n\n**Step 3.4:","new_string":"This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step). An important subtlety: the release script already has logic (at lines 366-385) to auto-resolve modify/delete merge conflicts on files in the `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` list. Once `\"docs/\"` is added, any docs changes on `develop` that conflict with the stripped `release/alpha` branch will be handled automatically. This is correct behavior and requires no additional code.\n\n**Step 3.4:"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1859,"cache_read_input_tokens":100373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1859},"output_tokens":394,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"2d2ffa0f-84d6-4e07-9863-b2ed5d69ea86","timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:39:07.520Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MN6qfzqi3pY76WMH2a1GqP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"ec559e09-b91b-438e-a441-9f6a56cf5758","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","oldString":"This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step).\n\n**Step 3.4:","newString":"This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step). An important subtlety: the release script already has logic (at lines 366-385) to auto-resolve modify/delete merge conflicts on files in the `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` list. Once `\"docs/\"` is added, any docs changes on `develop` that conflict with the stripped `release/alpha` branch will be handled automatically. This is correct behavior and requires no additional code.\n\n**Step 3.4:","originalFile":"# Plan: Migrate Hankweave to Monorepo\n\n## a. The Main Task\n\nConsolidate the `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` (runtime) and `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` (documentation site) repositories into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime package stays at the repository root. The docs site moves in as a workspace at `docs/`, flattened from its current `nextra-site/` subdirectory. The existing CI/CD pipelines, release process, public sync workflow, and Vercel docs deployment continue to function with targeted, minimal changes.\n\n---\n\n## b. Information Available\n\n### Sources that informed this plan\n\n1. **Task specification** -- `plan/task.md` (task description, open questions, research on Bun workspaces, Turborepo, and git subtree merges).\n2. **Opus plan and addendums** -- `plan/rough-workspace/opus/plan.md`, `addendum-docs.md`, `addendum-tests.md`, `log.md`. Detailed, phase-by-phase plan with exact file diffs, SOP drafts, and edge case analysis.\n3. **Codex plan and addendums** -- `plan/rough-workspace/codex/plan.md`, `addendum-1.md` (tests/CI), `addendum-2.md` (docs/deployment). Shorter plan with a notable catch on the `transformPackageJson()` gap for stripping `\"workspaces\"` from the public `package.json`.\n4. **Full source code review** -- Every config, script, workflow, and representative server/test file from both `source/hankweave/` and `source/hankweave-docs/`.\n\n### What I could see\n\n- Full directory structure and file contents of both repos.\n- All CI workflows (ci.yml, release.yml, sync-public.yml), composite actions (setup-environment, run-tests, dump-test-logs), and scripts (build.ts, build-executable.ts, release.ts, sync-public.ts, generate-schemas.ts, test-sync-local.ts, e2e/init.ts, run-cross-runtime-tests.ts).\n- Both `package.json` files, both `tsconfig.json` files, `biome.json`, `bunfig.toml`.\n- The full docs Nextra/Next.js setup including `vercel.json`, `next.config.mjs`, `app/`, `content/`, `components/`, `public/`, `styles/`.\n- The SOP document (`standard-operating-procedures.md`).\n- The `.gitignore` files from both repos.\n\n### What I could NOT see\n\n- The actual GitHub repos (branch protection rules, secrets, default branches, collaborator list).\n- The Vercel project dashboard settings (current root directory config, branch deployment rules).\n- The `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` (public mirror) repo contents -- only references to it in scripts and workflows.\n- Linear project / ticket context (no ticket ID provided).\n- Whether there are other repos or tools beyond what's in the source snapshot that the task spec's \"related packages/tools\" refers to.\n\n### Assumptions\n\n1. The `hankweave-docs` repo does not have significant git history worth preserving. The task spec describes history preservation as \"nice to have.\"\n2. The public mirror (`hankweave-runtime`) continues to exist as a separate repo. This migration consolidates the two private development repos only.\n3. The docs site continues to deploy to Vercel, now from the monorepo.\n4. No Turborepo or other task orchestration is needed for two packages.\n5. The `hankweave-docs/` outer wrapper (README, `notes/`, `plan/`) is development scaffolding that does not need to be carried into the monorepo.\n\n---\n\n## c. Sources and Related Things\n\n### Original task\n\n- Task description: `plan/task.md`\n- No Linear ticket ID provided.\n\n### Code references\n\n| File | Line(s) | Relevance |\n|------|---------|-----------|\n| `source/hankweave/package.json` | Full | Root package.json -- needs `workspaces` field added |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/package.json` | Full | Docs package.json -- moves to `docs/package.json` |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | 24-32 | The only cross-repo code dependency; `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | 76 | `docsAvailable` check -- will become permanently true |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/sync-public.ts` | 28 | `STRIP_DIRS` -- needs `\"docs\"` added |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/sync-public.ts` | 173-196 | `transformPackageJson()` -- needs to strip `\"workspaces\"` |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/release.ts` | 54-60 | `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` -- needs `\"docs/\"` added |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | 160-175 | `shouldNotExist` verification list -- needs `\"docs\"` added |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Full | CI workflow -- minimal changes needed |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/release.yml` | Full | Release workflow -- minimal changes |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/sync-public.yml` | Full | Sync workflow -- no code changes needed |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml` | 34 | `bun install --frozen-lockfile` -- works with workspaces |\n| `source/hankweave/biome.json` | 4-11 | Linting scope whitelist -- only covers runtime files |\n| `source/hankweave/bunfig.toml` | Full | Bun config -- no changes needed |\n| `source/hankweave/tsconfig.json` | Full | Runtime TS config -- stays as-is |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/tsconfig.json` | Full | Docs TS config -- stays as-is at new location |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/vercel.json` | Full | Vercel config -- stays in docs workspace |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/next.config.mjs` | Full | Next.js config -- no changes |\n| `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md` | 10-30, 31-40, 337-354 | Repo structure, strip list docs, key files |\n| `source/hankweave/.gitignore` | Full | May need additions for docs build artifacts |\n| `source/hankweave/server/utils.ts` | 402-410 | `getMetadata()` reads `../package.json` -- structural assumption |\n\n### Research sources\n\n- [Bun Workspaces](https://bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces) -- native workspace support via `\"workspaces\"` field in `package.json`\n- [Bun Catalogs](https://bun.sh/docs/install/catalogs) -- optional shared dependency versioning (not needed initially)\n- [Git subtree merges](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/using-git/about-git-subtree-merges) -- for preserving docs repo history\n\n---\n\n## d. Conventions and Patterns\n\n### Observed code conventions\n\n1. **Scripts are TypeScript.** All build/release/sync scripts are `.ts` files run with `bun`.\n2. **Relative paths from `import.meta.dir`.** Scripts use `path.join(import.meta.dir, \"..\")` to resolve project root.\n3. **`Bun.spawn` for shell commands.** Scripts use `Bun.spawn([\"sh\", \"-c\", cmd])`.\n4. **Two-space indent, 100-char line width.** Enforced by Biome.\n5. **LF line endings.** Enforced by `.gitattributes`.\n6. **No shared state between packages.** Docs don't import from runtime; only schema JSON files are copied by a script.\n7. **Strip lists are explicit.** Both `sync-public.ts` and `release.ts` maintain explicit lists of files/dirs to remove. Adding a new internal directory means adding it to both.\n8. **Runtime is strict ESM TypeScript** with explicit `.js` import specifiers (e.g., `import \"./utils.js\"`).\n9. **`server/utils.ts` reads `../package.json`** for version metadata. This assumes `server/` is one level below the package root.\n\n### Patterns to follow\n\n- Add `\"docs\"` to existing strip lists rather than creating new mechanisms.\n- Keep the root `package.json` as the runtime's `package.json` (add only the `\"workspaces\"` field).\n- Don't introduce Turborepo or other tooling -- Bun workspaces is sufficient for two packages.\n- Keep separate `tsconfig.json` per workspace (they have incompatible settings: runtime targets ES2022 with strict mode and bun-types; docs targets ES2020 with strict disabled and Next.js plugin).\n- Don't introduce `workspace:*` dependencies between docs and runtime. The schema copy is a script-level file operation, not a package dependency.\n\n### Patterns to avoid\n\n- Don't move the runtime into a subdirectory. This would break dozens of paths across scripts, CI workflows, and `server/utils.ts` metadata resolution.\n- Don't create a shared `tsconfig.base.json`. The two configs are too different.\n- Don't add workspace filter flags to CI scripts. For two packages, let everything install and run from root.\n- Don't extend `biome.json` to cover `docs/`. The docs site uses React/JSX conventions and Next.js tooling that are not part of the runtime's Biome setup.\n\n---\n\n## e. Decision Points and Judgement Calls\n\n### Decision 1: Keep the runtime at the repo root\n\n**Chosen**: The runtime stays at root. The docs site moves into `docs/`.\n\n**Reasoning**: The runtime has 8 scripts, 3 CI workflows, 3 composite actions, build/release/sync pipelines, and extensive relative path usage (scripts use `import.meta.dir` + `\"..\"`, `server/utils.ts` reads `../package.json`, build scripts use `\"./server/index.ts\"` as entry point). Moving it into a subdirectory would require changing every one of these. The docs site has no CI of its own, no complex scripts, and a single `package.json`.\n\n**Trade-off**: The root `package.json` serves dual purpose as both workspace root and runtime package. This is a recognized Bun workspace pattern -- the root package is an \"implicit workspace member\" by default.\n\n**Alternative considered**: Both packages in `packages/` subdirectories. This is the conventional monorepo layout but would be a massive path-rewrite refactor (build scripts, CI workflows, composite actions, `import.meta.dir` references, `server/utils.ts` metadata resolution). Not justified for two packages.\n\n### Decision 2: Flatten the docs into `docs/`\n\n**Chosen**: Move `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/*` contents directly into `docs/` (not `docs/nextra-site/` or `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`).\n\n**Reasoning**: The `nextra-site/` wrapper exists because the docs repo has a root with README, `notes/`, and `plan/` directories. In the monorepo, these don't need a separate layer. Flattening gives a clean workspace path (`\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]`), shorter references everywhere, and follows common conventions where `docs/` is a well-understood directory name.\n\n**Alternative considered**: Keeping `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` intact (the Codex recommendation). This preserves the original structure verbatim but results in the awkward path `\"workspaces\": [\"hankweave-docs/nextra-site\"]` and an unnecessary depth of nesting. Every reference to the docs workspace becomes longer.\n\n**What happens to `hankweave-docs/` non-nextra files**: The `README.md` at docs repo root is optional and can be included as `docs/README.md` or discarded. The `notes/` and `plan/` directories are historical development artifacts -- discard them. If the team wants them preserved, archive in `intermediates/` (e.g., `intermediates/docs-migration-legacy/`).\n\n### Decision 3: No `workspace:*` dependencies\n\n**Chosen**: No workspace dependency between docs and runtime.\n\n**Reasoning**: The docs site doesn't `import` anything from `@southbridgeai/hankweave`. The only data flow is schema JSON files copied by `generate-schemas.ts`. This is a script-level file copy, not a package dependency. Adding `workspace:*` would incorrectly suggest the docs depend on the runtime as a library.\n\n**When to revisit**: If the docs ever need to import TypeScript types or utilities from the runtime (e.g., for auto-generated API reference), add `workspace:*` at that point.\n\n### Decision 4: Convert the existing hankweave repo, don't create new\n\n**Chosen**: Modify `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` in-place to become the monorepo.\n\n**Reasoning**: All CI workflows, GitHub secrets, branch protection rules, Linear integration, and team permissions are already configured on this repo. Creating a new repo would require reconfiguring everything. The existing git history stays intact. The docs files are brought in via a merge commit (or `git subtree add` if history preservation is desired).\n\n### Decision 5: No Turborepo\n\n**Chosen**: Use Bun workspaces alone.\n\n**Reasoning**: Two packages don't need task orchestration or caching. The runtime builds and tests independently. The docs site builds independently on Vercel. There's no dependency chain requiring `^build` semantics. Adding Turborepo would increase complexity with no clear benefit.\n\n**When to revisit**: If more packages are added (e.g., a shared types package, a CLI package), or if CI times become problematic and caching would help.\n\n### Decision 6: Single lockfile at root\n\n**Chosen**: One `bun.lock` at the repo root, replacing both existing lockfiles.\n\n**Reasoning**: Bun workspaces uses a single root lockfile. Both workspace packages' dependencies are resolved and locked together. The first `bun install` after migration regenerates this. The docs-side `bun.lock` (from `nextra-site/`) is deleted.\n\n### Decision 7: Strip `\"workspaces\"` from public `package.json`\n\n**Chosen**: Modify `transformPackageJson()` in `sync-public.ts` to delete `pkg.workspaces` before writing the public `package.json`.\n\n**Reasoning**: The public mirror will not contain the `docs/` directory (it's stripped by `STRIP_DIRS`). If the public `package.json` ships with `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]`, it references a directory that doesn't exist, which is confusing and could cause unexpected behavior when someone runs `bun install` or `npm install` on the public repo. This was identified by the Codex plan and confirmed by code review -- the current `transformPackageJson()` function (at `sync-public.ts:173-196`) changes `name`, `publishConfig`, `homepage`, and strips some scripts, but does not touch `workspaces`.\n\n### Over/under engineering line\n\n- **Under (acceptable)**: Not adding `paths:` filtering to CI triggers. Docs changes trigger runtime tests, but CI runs are fast enough that this isn't worth the complexity for two packages.\n- **Under (acceptable)**: Not using Bun catalogs for shared TypeScript version. The projects only share TypeScript as a dev dependency and can version independently.\n- **Over (avoid)**: Adding Turborepo, shared tsconfig base, workspace link scripts, or monorepo-specific CI orchestration tooling.\n- **Right level**: Adding `\"docs\"` to strip lists, updating one path in `generate-schemas.ts`, updating the SOP, stripping `\"workspaces\"` from public package.json. Minimal changes that make the monorepo work correctly.\n\n---\n\n## f. The Actual Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 0: Preparation\n\n**Step 0.1: Create a feature branch**\n```bash\ngit checkout develop\ngit pull origin develop\ngit checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration\n```\n\n**Step 0.2: Verify clean state**\n```bash\nbun run test:unit\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\ngit status  # must be clean\n```\n\n### Phase 1: Bring docs into the repo\n\n**Step 1.1: Create the `docs/` directory**\n\nCopy the contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/` at the runtime repo root. The files to bring in:\n\n```\napp/\ncomponents/\ncontent/\npublic/\nstyles/\nbun.lock           (will be removed in step 1.3)\nmdx-components.tsx\nnext-env.d.ts\nnext.config.mjs\npackage.json\ntsconfig.json\nvercel.json\n```\n\nDo NOT copy the outer `hankweave-docs/` wrapper (`notes/`, `plan/`). Optionally include `hankweave-docs/README.md` as `docs/README.md` for internal reference.\n\nIf git history preservation is desired, use `git subtree add`:\n```bash\ngit remote add -f hankweave-docs <url>\ngit merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories hankweave-docs/main\ngit read-tree --prefix=docs/ -u hankweave-docs/main\ngit commit -m \"Merge hankweave-docs into monorepo as docs workspace\"\n```\nThen restructure: move `docs/nextra-site/*` up to `docs/` and remove `docs/notes/`, `docs/plan/`, `docs/README.md`, `docs/.gitignore`.\n\nAlternatively, a simple file copy with a descriptive commit is simpler and the docs repo history remains available in the original repo if ever needed.\n\n**Step 1.2: Add workspace configuration to root `package.json`**\n\nAdd the `\"workspaces\"` field to `source/hankweave/package.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@southbridgeai/hankweave\",\n  \"version\": \"0.5.6\",\n  \"workspaces\": [\"docs\"],\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nThe root package is itself an implicit workspace member in Bun workspaces, so the runtime's own dependencies, scripts, and `\"files\"` field continue to work unchanged.\n\n**Step 1.3: Delete the docs-side `bun.lock`**\n\nRemove `docs/bun.lock`. The root lockfile manages all dependencies.\n\n**Step 1.4: Run `bun install`**\n\nFrom the repo root:\n```bash\nbun install\n```\n\nThis resolves dependencies for both workspaces, generates a new unified `bun.lock` at root, and creates a single hoisted `node_modules/` tree. The docs dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, etc.) will be added to the root lockfile but should not conflict with the runtime's dependencies -- the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees.\n\n**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n```\n\nVerify the Next.js build succeeds. The `postbuild` step (Pagefind search indexing) should also run. If there are module resolution issues, they'll surface here.\n\n### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n\n**Step 2.1: Update `scripts/generate-schemas.ts`**\n\nChange the `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path (lines 24-32) from:\n```typescript\nconst DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR = path.join(\n  import.meta.dir,\n  \"..\",\n  \"..\",\n  \"hankweave-docs\",\n  \"nextra-site\",\n  \"public\",\n  \"schemas\",\n);\n```\n\nTo:\n```typescript\nconst DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR = path.join(\n  import.meta.dir,\n  \"..\",\n  \"docs\",\n  \"public\",\n  \"schemas\",\n);\n```\n\nThe `docsAvailable` check at line 76 (`fs.existsSync(path.dirname(DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR))`) will now always evaluate to true since `docs/public/` is always present in the monorepo. Keep the check for defensive safety -- it doesn't hurt, and it means the script still works correctly if someone runs it from an unexpected working directory.\n\n**Step 2.2: Run schema generation to verify**\n\n```bash\nbun run generate-schemas\nls schemas/hank.schema.json\nls docs/public/schemas/hank.schema.json\n```\n\nVerify schemas are written to both `schemas/` (runtime's local copy for npm) and `docs/public/schemas/` (docs site's static files).\n\n### Phase 3: Update strip lists for public sync\n\nThis phase has four changes across three scripts, plus an update to the `transformPackageJson()` function. All serve the same purpose: ensure the docs workspace doesn't leak into the public mirror.\n\n**Step 3.1: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `STRIP_DIRS`**\n\nAt line 28, add `\"docs\"`:\n```typescript\nconst STRIP_DIRS = [\"intermediates\", \"external-docs\", \"public-release-files\", \".github/actions\", \"docs\"];\n```\n\n**Step 3.2: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `transformPackageJson()`**\n\nAt line 173-196 in the `transformPackageJson()` function, add a line to delete the `\"workspaces\"` field from the public `package.json`:\n\n```typescript\nasync function transformPackageJson(packagePath: string): Promise<void> {\n  const content = await readFile(packagePath, \"utf-8\");\n  const pkg = JSON.parse(content);\n\n  pkg.name = \"hankweave\";\n  pkg.publishConfig = { access: \"public\" };\n  pkg.homepage = \"https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime\";\n\n  // Remove monorepo-only fields that don't apply to the public repo\n  delete pkg.workspaces;\n\n  // Remove scripts that reference stripped internal files\n  if (pkg.scripts) {\n    for (const script of STRIP_SCRIPTS) {\n      delete pkg.scripts[script];\n    }\n  }\n\n  await writeFile(packagePath, JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n  // ... logging\n}\n```\n\nThis is critical. Without it, the public `package.json` would contain `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` pointing to a directory that doesn't exist in the public mirror.\n\n**Step 3.3: Update `scripts/release.ts` `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP`**\n\nAt line 54, add `\"docs/\"`:\n```typescript\nconst INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP = [\n  \"intermediates/\",\n  \"external-docs/\",\n  \"CLAUDE.md\",\n  \"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\n  \"standard-operating-procedures.md\",\n  \"docs/\",\n];\n```\n\nThis ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step).\n\n**Step 3.4: Update `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` `shouldNotExist`**\n\nAt line 160, add `\"docs\"` to the verification list:\n```typescript\nconst shouldNotExist = [\n  \"intermediates\",\n  \"external-docs\",\n  \"CLAUDE.md\",\n  \"Claude.md\",\n  \"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\n  \"PUBLISHING-PLAN.md\",\n  \"public-release-files\",\n  \".github/actions\",\n  \"scripts/sync-public.ts\",\n  \"scripts/test-sync-local.ts\",\n  \"scripts/release.ts\",\n  \"telemetry.md\",\n  \"standard-operating-procedures.md\",\n  \".github/workflows/ci.yml\",\n  \"docs\",\n];\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Update `.gitignore`\n\n**Step 4.1: Merge docs-specific ignores into root `.gitignore`**\n\nAdd the following to the root `.gitignore`:\n\n```gitignore\n# Docs build output\ndocs/.next/\ndocs/out/\n\n# Pagefind search index (generated at build time)\ndocs/public/_pagefind/\n```\n\nMost entries from the docs `.gitignore` (like `node_modules/`, `.env`, `.DS_Store`) are already covered by the root `.gitignore`. The root `.gitignore` already has a generic `.next` and `out` entry (lines 141-142: `.next` and `out`), but since those are not scoped to `docs/`, they'd match those directories anywhere in the tree including at root. The `docs/`-prefixed versions are more explicit but the existing generic entries already cover the docs case. The Pagefind `_pagefind/` pattern is docs-specific and should be added.\n\nOne note: the root `.gitignore` already has `dist` at line 147 (under the `.nuxt` section), which would match `docs/dist/` too. No additional entry needed for that.\n\n### Phase 5: Update documentation\n\n**Step 5.1: Update `standard-operating-procedures.md` -- Repository Structure (Section 1)**\n\nUpdate the directory tree at lines 10-27 to include `docs/`:\n\n```\nhankweave-dev/              <- private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n├── server/                 <- runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n├── scripts/                <- build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n├── tests/                  <- unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n├── schemas/                <- generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n├── shims/                  <- agent harness adapters\n├── docs/                   <- documentation site workspace (Next.js + Nextra)\n│   ├── app/                <- Next.js app directory\n│   ├── content/            <- MDX documentation pages\n│   ├── components/         <- custom React components\n│   ├── public/             <- static assets + generated schemas\n│   └── package.json        <- hankweave-docs workspace\n├── learning/               <- example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n├── intermediates/          <- planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n├── external-docs/          <- SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n├── public-release-files/   <- files overlaid onto the public repo during sync\n├── assets/                 <- images, demo GIFs\n├── .github/                <- CI workflows and composite actions\n├── CHANGELOG.md            <- Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n├── CONTRIBUTING.md         <- branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n└── package.json            <- @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm) + workspace root\n```\n\nAdd a note below the tree:\n\n```\nThe documentation site (`docs/`) deploys to Vercel from this repo. It is a Bun workspace\nbut does not have a workspace dependency on the runtime package.\n```\n\n**Step 5.2: Update \"What gets stripped\" section (lines 31-40)**\n\nAdd `docs/` to the directories list:\n\n```\n- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`, `docs/`\n```\n\nAlso add a note that `\"workspaces\"` is stripped from `package.json` during public sync transformation.\n\n**Step 5.3: Update Key Files Reference (Section 9, lines 337-354)**\n\nAdd docs workspace entries:\n\n```\n| `docs/package.json`         | Documentation site workspace (hankweave-docs)              |\n| `docs/content/`             | MDX documentation pages (concepts, guides, reference)      |\n```\n\n**Step 5.4: Add Documentation site note to Development Workflow (Section 3)**\n\nAdd a subsection:\n\n```markdown\n### Documentation site\n\nThe documentation site is a Bun workspace at `docs/`. To work on it locally:\n\n    cd docs && bun run dev    # Development server with hot reload\n    cd docs && bun run build  # Production build\n\nChanges to docs pages (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`) deploy automatically via Vercel when\npushed to the configured branch.\n\nSchema generation writes to both `schemas/` (for the npm package) and\n`docs/public/schemas/` (for the docs site):\n\n    bun run generate-schemas\n```\n\n### Phase 6: Verify everything works\n\n**Step 6.1: Run the full test suite**\n```bash\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\nbun run test:unit\nbun run test:integration\n```\n\nNone of these should be affected by the migration. The runtime code is unchanged, test imports use relative paths from `tests/` to `server/`, and Biome's `includes` whitelist only covers runtime files.\n\n**Step 6.2: Run schema generation**\n```bash\nbun run generate-schemas\n```\nVerify output exists in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n\n**Step 6.3: Run the runtime build**\n```bash\nbun run build\n```\nVerify `dist/index.js` is created. The build script uses `import.meta.dir` relative paths and `\"./server/index.ts\"` as entry point -- these are all unaffected by the workspace addition.\n\n**Step 6.4: Verify docs build**\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n```\nVerify Next.js build succeeds and the `postbuild` Pagefind step runs.\n\n**Step 6.5: Verify npm pack excludes docs**\n```bash\nnpm pack --dry-run\n```\nVerify the tarball file list contains only `dist/`, `shims/`, `schemas/`, and metadata files. The `docs/` directory should NOT appear because it's not in the `\"files\"` allowlist.\n\n**Step 6.6: Test the sync dry-run**\n```bash\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <current-version> --use-head\n```\nVerify:\n- `docs/` is correctly stripped from the snapshot\n- `\"workspaces\"` is removed from the public `package.json`\n- All existing verification checks pass (the `shouldNotExist` and `shouldExist` lists)\n\n**Step 6.7: Test release dry-run (if on develop with clean tree)**\n```bash\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n```\nVerify validation passes. This exercises the merge feasibility check which now includes `\"docs/\"` in `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP`.\n\n### Phase 7: Vercel configuration (out-of-band)\n\nThis is a manual change in the Vercel dashboard, not a code change.\n\n**Step 7.1: Update Vercel project settings**\n\n1. Go to the Vercel project for `hankweave-docs`.\n2. Under \"Git\" -> \"Connected Git Repository\", change from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`.\n3. Set \"Root Directory\" to `docs`.\n4. Verify the Framework Preset is still \"Next.js\".\n5. The `vercel.json` inside `docs/` will continue to work (it specifies `\"framework\": \"nextjs\"`, `\"installCommand\": \"bun install\"`, `\"buildCommand\": \"bun run build\"`).\n\n**Step 7.2: Install behavior consideration**\n\nThe `vercel.json` `installCommand` is `\"bun install\"`, which runs from the Vercel-configured root directory (`docs/`). Because `docs/` is a workspace member, Bun should look upward for the workspace root's `package.json` and install the full workspace dependency tree. However, if Vercel only mounts the subdirectory (not the full repo), workspace resolution may fail.\n\nFallback: If workspace resolution fails in Vercel, change the Vercel root directory to `/` (repo root) and update the commands:\n- `installCommand`: `\"bun install\"` (at root -- installs all workspaces)\n- `buildCommand`: `\"cd docs && bun run build\"`\n\n**Step 7.3: Configure \"Ignored Build Step\" (recommended)**\n\nTo prevent unnecessary docs rebuilds when only runtime code changes:\n1. Go to Settings -> General -> \"Ignored Build Step\"\n2. Set to: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n\nThis tells Vercel to skip the build if no files under `docs/` have changed.\n\n**Step 7.4: Configure branch deployment**\n\nThe monorepo uses `develop` and `release/alpha` branches. Configure Vercel:\n- Production deployment: whichever branch the docs should deploy from (likely `develop` or `release/alpha`, depending on team preference)\n- Preview deployments: PRs targeting `develop`\n\n### Phase 8: Cleanup and commit\n\n**Step 8.1: Archive the old `hankweave-docs` repo (after migration is verified)**\n\nAfter the monorepo migration is merged and Vercel is confirmed working:\n1. Archive `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` on GitHub (set to read-only).\n2. Update the README to say \"This repo has been merged into SouthBridgeAI/hankweave.\"\n3. Disconnect Vercel from the old repo (after the new connection is verified).\n\n**Step 8.2: Commit the migration**\n\nCommit all changes on the feature branch:\n```\nMigrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n\n- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- Strip \"workspaces\" from public package.json in transformPackageJson()\n- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n```\n\n**Step 8.3: Open PR targeting develop**\n\nFollow the existing PR conventions per SOP Section 4:\n- Title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n- Body: Problem/approach/files-changed format\n\n**Step 8.4: Optional CHANGELOG entry**\n\nUnder `[Unreleased] > Changed`:\n```markdown\n- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\nThis is optional since it's an internal infrastructure change, not user-facing.\n\n---\n\n## g. Testing Considerations\n\n### Existing tests affected\n\n**None.** No existing test file needs modification. The migration changes the root `package.json` (adds `\"workspaces\"`), scripts in `scripts/` (path adjustments, strip list updates), `.gitignore`, and the SOP document. None of these are read by tests.\n\nSpecifically checked:\n- `tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts` reads from `schemas/` which is unchanged.\n- `tests/unit/config.test.ts` reads from `server/config.ts` which is unchanged.\n- `tests/unit/utils.test.ts` uses `getMetadata()` which reads version from `package.json` -- the `\"workspaces\"` field won't affect this.\n- All test imports use relative paths from `tests/` to `server/` which are unaffected.\n\n### New tests needed\n\nNo new automated tests are strictly required. The migration is a structural change, not a code change. Verification is manual (Phase 6 above).\n\nOptional: A lightweight monorepo smoke test could be added:\n```typescript\n// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\nimport { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\n\ndescribe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n\n  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs schemas directory exists\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nThis is a small structural invariant check. Only add if the team wants structural tests.\n\n### Edge cases to cover\n\n1. **`bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI.** The new unified `bun.lock` must be committed. If it's missing, CI's `--frozen-lockfile` flag will fail. This is the composite action at `.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml:34`.\n\n2. **npm publish from root.** The `\"files\"` field (`[\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]`) is an allowlist. `docs/` is not listed, so it won't be in the npm tarball. Verify with `npm pack --dry-run`.\n\n3. **Dependency hoisting conflicts.** Bun workspaces hoists dependencies. The runtime and docs have almost entirely different dependency trees (server-side Bun tools vs. React/Next.js), so conflicts are unlikely. The only shared dev dependency is `typescript`, which can safely have independent versions per workspace.\n\n4. **Build executable.** `build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and builds from root. This path doesn't change with workspace addition.\n\n5. **Cross-runtime tests.** `run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. This path doesn't change.\n\n6. **Cross-platform path separators.** The CI matrix includes Windows, macOS, and Linux. Workspace paths are resolved by Bun which handles path separators. No issues expected, but worth monitoring the first CI run after migration.\n\n### CI enhancement (optional, recommended)\n\nConsider adding a docs build step to CI to prevent monorepo PRs from silently breaking docs:\n\n```yaml\n# In ci.yml, add a new job:\ndocs-build:\n  name: Docs Build Check\n  runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n  timeout-minutes: 10\n  steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - uses: ./.github/actions/setup-environment\n      with:\n        install-gemini: \"false\"\n    - name: Build docs\n      run: cd docs && bun run build\n```\n\nThis is a nice-to-have. Without it, a broken docs build would only be caught by Vercel deployment failures, not by the PR CI checks.\n\n---\n\n## h. Documentation Considerations\n\n### Docs to update\n\n1. **`standard-operating-procedures.md`** -- Repository structure diagram, strip list documentation, key files reference, development workflow section. Detailed in Phase 5 above.\n2. **This plan itself** -- Should be filed as an intermediate (e.g., `intermediates/45-monorepo-migration/`).\n\n### New docs needed\n\nNone required. The monorepo migration is an internal infrastructure change. The user-facing docs (`docs/content/`) document Hankweave as a CLI tool, not the development repo structure.\n\n### Docs that should NOT be updated\n\n- User-facing docs (`docs/content/guides/getting-started.mdx`, etc.) -- these reference `hankweave` as a CLI tool, not a repo layout.\n- The public `README.md` (in `public-release-files/`) -- describes the public `hankweave-runtime` repo.\n- The `CHANGELOG.md` -- unless the team wants the optional internal note described in Phase 8.\n\n---\n\n## i. Additional Resources\n\n### Bun workspaces\n\n- [bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces](https://bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces) -- primary reference\n- Root package can be a workspace member itself (important for the \"runtime at root\" approach)\n- `bun install` at root installs all workspace dependencies\n- `bun --filter <name> <script>` runs scripts in specific workspaces (useful for `bun --filter hankweave-docs build`)\n\n### Vercel monorepo support\n\n- Vercel's \"Root Directory\" setting specifies which subdirectory contains the deployable project\n- \"Ignored Build Step\" filters deploys to only relevant changes\n- Vercel handles Bun workspaces when it can see the full repo tree\n\n### Git subtree (optional history preservation)\n\n```bash\ngit remote add -f hankweave-docs <url>\ngit merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories hankweave-docs/main\ngit read-tree --prefix=docs/ -u hankweave-docs/main\ngit commit -m \"Merge hankweave-docs into monorepo as docs workspace\"\n```\n\nThis preserves the full commit history of `hankweave-docs` at the `docs/` prefix. After this, restructure so the `nextra-site/` contents are at `docs/` root and remove unwanted wrapper files.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n| File | Change Type | Description |\n|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `package.json` | Modify | Add `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` |\n| `docs/` | Create (directory) | Contains flattened contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` |\n| `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | Modify | Update `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path (lines 24-32) |\n| `scripts/sync-public.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs\"` to `STRIP_DIRS` (line 28); add `delete pkg.workspaces` to `transformPackageJson()` |\n| `scripts/release.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs/\"` to `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` (line 54) |\n| `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs\"` to `shouldNotExist` (line 160) |\n| `.gitignore` | Modify | Add docs build artifacts (`docs/public/_pagefind/`) |\n| `standard-operating-procedures.md` | Modify | Update repo structure, strip list, key files, add docs section |\n| `bun.lock` | Regenerate | New unified lockfile covering both workspaces |\n\n**Total files modified**: 7 existing files + 1 new directory (~30 files from docs)\n**Total lines of code changed**: ~25 lines across scripts and configs + SOP update\n\nThe migration's success is measured by how little changes while still achieving the goal: a reliable, explicit relationship between runtime and docs in a single repo, with the public sync pipeline continuing to produce correct output.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":363,"oldLines":7,"newStart":363,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ];"," ```"," ","-This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step).","+This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step). An important subtlety: the release script already has logic (at lines 366-385) to auto-resolve modify/delete merge conflicts on files in the `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` list. Once `\"docs/\"` is added, any docs changes on `develop` that conflict with the stripped `release/alpha` branch will be handled automatically. This is correct behavior and requires no additional code."," "," **Step 3.4: Update `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` `shouldNotExist`**"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:39:07.874Z"}
