{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MEH9FeVYJ9XZfMevizyQow","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Addendum: Testing Considerations\n     2→\n     3→*Read alongside `plan.md`. Covers test impact, test patterns, and what to verify after the monorepo migration.*\n     4→\n     5→---\n     6→\n     7→## 1. What the supplementary materials reveal\n     8→\n     9→### Test infrastructure overview\n    10→\n    11→The test suite is organized in four tiers:\n    12→\n    13→| Tier | Location | Runner | Count | External deps |\n    14→|------|----------|--------|-------|--------------|\n    15→| Unit | `tests/unit/` | `bun:test` | 65+ files | None |\n    16→| Integration | `tests/integration/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Mock LLM |\n    17→| E2E | `tests/e2e/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Real API keys |\n    18→| Cross-runtime | `tests/cross-runtime/` | `bun`/`node`/`deno` | 3+ files | None |\n    19→\n    20→All tests import from `../../server/<module>` using relative paths from within the `tests/` directory. Since the `server/` directory is not moving, **no test imports need to change**.\n    21→\n    22→### Test runner configuration\n    23→\n    24→- `bunfig.toml` sets `BUN_TEST=1` environment variable for test runs\n    25→- `package.json` defines test scripts: `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `test`, `test:e2e:init`, `test:cross-runtime:*`\n    26→- CI uses composite action `.github/actions/run-tests/action.yml` which calls `bun test tests/unit` and `bun test tests/integration`\n    27→\n    28→### Test utilities\n    29→\n    30→Key test utilities at `tests/utils/`:\n    31→- `sentinel-test-harness.ts` — mock LLM calls, event tracking, test workspace management\n    32→- `mock-llm.ts` — typed mock LLM provider with configurable responses\n    33→- `env-test-helpers.ts` — environment variable capture/restore for test isolation\n    34→\n    35→None of these reference paths outside the runtime package.\n    36→\n    37→---\n    38→\n    39→## 2. Existing tests affected by the planned changes\n    40→\n    41→### Directly affected: None\n    42→\n    43→No existing test file needs modification. The migration changes:\n    44→1. Root `package.json` (adds `workspaces` field)\n    45→2. Scripts in `scripts/` (path adjustments)\n    46→3. `.gitignore` (docs artifacts)\n    47→4. SOP document\n    48→\n    49→None of these are read by tests. The `tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts` reads from `schemas/` which is unchanged. The `tests/unit/config.test.ts` reads from `server/config.ts` which is unchanged.\n    50→\n    51→### Potentially affected (low risk)\n    52→\n    53→1. **`tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts`** — Tests that generated schemas validate correctly. The schemas themselves don't change, only where they're also copied to (now `docs/public/schemas/` instead of `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/`). The test reads from `schemas/` which is the runtime's local copy.\n    54→\n    55→2. **`tests/integration/schema-zod-parity.test.ts`** — Verifies Zod schemas match JSON schemas. Same as above — reads from `schemas/`, not affected.\n    56→\n    57→3. **Any test reading `package.json`** — The `\"workspaces\"` field addition shouldn't affect tests that read version or package name. Verified: `tests/unit/utils.test.ts` reads `getMetadata()` which extracts `name` and `version` from `package.json` — the `workspaces` field won't interfere.\n    58→\n    59→### Not affected: everything else\n    60→\n    61→All unit tests, integration tests, E2E tests, and cross-runtime tests operate on runtime code and mock data. They have no awareness of the docs workspace.\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→## 3. New tests to write\n    66→\n    67→### No new automated tests are strictly required\n    68→\n    69→The migration is a structural change (directory layout, workspace configuration) rather than a code change. The runtime behavior is identical before and after migration.\n    70→\n    71→### Recommended manual verification checklist\n    72→\n    73→After migration, verify by hand (or in a CI validation step):\n    74→\n    75→```bash\n    76→# 1. Workspace installs correctly\n    77→bun install\n    78→# Expected: success, single bun.lock at root, docs/node_modules linked\n    79→\n    80→# 2. Runtime tests still pass\n    81→bun run test:unit\n    82→bun run test:integration\n    83→bun run lint\n    84→bun run tc\n    85→\n    86→# 3. Schema generation writes to both locations\n    87→bun run generate-schemas\n    88→ls schemas/hank-file.schema.json\n    89→ls docs/public/schemas/hank-file.schema.json\n    90→\n    91→# 4. Runtime build works\n    92→bun run build\n    93→ls dist/index.js\n    94→\n    95→# 5. Docs build works\n    96→cd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n    97→\n    98→# 6. npm pack excludes docs\n    99→npm pack --dry-run\n   100→# Expected: docs/ NOT in the file list\n   101→\n   102→# 7. Sync dry-run strips docs correctly (requires git history)\n   103→bun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <version> --use-head\n   104→# Expected: \"Correctly removed: docs\" in verification output\n   105→```\n   106→\n   107→### Optional: Add a workspace smoke test\n   108→\n   109→If desired, a lightweight test could be added to verify the monorepo structure is consistent:\n   110→\n   111→```typescript\n   112→// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\n   113→import { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\n   114→import * as fs from \"node:fs\";\n   115→import * as path from \"node:path\";\n   116→\n   117→describe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n   118→  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n   119→\n   120→  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n   121→    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n   122→    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n   123→  });\n   124→\n   125→  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n   126→    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n   127→  });\n   128→\n   129→  test(\"docs schemas directory exists\", () => {\n   130→    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\"))).toBe(true);\n   131→  });\n   132→});\n   133→```\n   134→\n   135→This is lightweight and validates the structural invariant. Optional — only add if the team wants structural tests.\n   136→\n   137→---\n   138→\n   139→## 4. Edge cases to cover\n   140→\n   141→### 4.1: `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI\n   142→\n   143→After migration, the CI composite action (`.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml:34`) runs:\n   144→```bash\n   145→bun install --frozen-lockfile\n   146→```\n   147→\n   148→This will fail if the `bun.lock` at root doesn't include the docs workspace's dependencies. **The `bun.lock` must be regenerated and committed as part of the migration.**\n   149→\n   150→### 4.2: The docs workspace's `devDependencies` in the root lockfile\n   151→\n   152→The docs workspace has these dependencies that the runtime doesn't:\n   153→- `next` ^15.0.0\n   154→- `nextra` ^4.0.0\n   155→- `nextra-theme-docs` ^4.0.0\n   156→- `react` ^19.0.0\n   157→- `react-dom` ^19.0.0\n   158→- `@vercel/analytics` ^1.6.1\n   159→- `posthog-js` ^1.347.2\n   160→- `pagefind` ^1.3.0\n   161→\n   162→These will be added to the root `bun.lock`. They should NOT conflict with the runtime's dependencies. The runtime doesn't use React or Next.js. The only shared dependency is `typescript` — both packages use it but can have independent versions.\n   163→\n   164→### 4.3: `npm publish` from root\n   165→\n   166→The `release.yml` runs `npm publish` from the repo root. The `\"files\"` field in `package.json`:\n   167→```json\n   168→\"files\": [\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]\n   169→```\n   170→\n   171→This is an allowlist — `docs/` won't be included. Verify with `npm pack --dry-run` that the published tarball doesn't include docs workspace files.\n   172→\n   173→### 4.4: Build executable with workspace\n   174→\n   175→`build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and builds from root. Bun's build should resolve the entry point the same way with or without workspaces. Verify: `bun scripts/build-executable.ts` produces a working binary.\n   176→\n   177→### 4.5: Cross-runtime tests\n   178→\n   179→`scripts/run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. This path doesn't change. Cross-runtime tests import from `../../server/` which doesn't change. Should work without modification.\n   180→\n   181→---\n   182→\n   183→## 5. Test patterns and conventions to follow\n   184→\n   185→If adding any new tests (e.g., the optional monorepo structure test):\n   186→\n   187→1. **Location**: `tests/unit/` for unit tests, `tests/integration/` for integration\n   188→2. **Import style**: `import { ... } from \"bun:test\"` for test framework, `import * as fs from \"node:fs\"` for Node APIs\n   189→3. **Relative imports**: `../../server/<module>` from test files\n   190→4. **Cleanup**: Create temp directories, clean up in `afterEach`/`afterAll`\n   191→5. **No global state**: Each test should be independent\n   192→6. **Biome compliance**: Tests in `tests/unit/` and `tests/e2e/` are covered by Biome linting\n   193→\n   194→---\n   195→\n   196→## 6. Conflicts or inconsistencies\n   197→\n   198→**None identified.** The plan and test infrastructure are consistent. The migration doesn't touch any runtime code, so all existing tests should pass without modification.\n   199→\n   200→The only \"inconsistency\" worth noting: the `generate-schemas.ts` script currently silently skips writing to docs if the path doesn't exist (`docsAvailable` check). After migration, this path will always exist, so the `docsAvailable` check becomes redundant. The plan recommends keeping the check (defensive) rather than removing it (premature cleanup).\n   201→\n   202→---\n   203→\n   204→## 7. Risks\n   205→\n   206→1. **Dependency hoisting conflicts**: Bun workspaces hoists dependencies. If the runtime and docs have conflicting versions of a shared transitive dependency, the hoist could cause issues. This is unlikely — the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees (server-side Bun tools vs. React/Next.js).\n   207→\n   208→2. **CI time increase**: CI now installs docs dependencies even when only runtime code changed. This adds maybe 10-20 seconds to `bun install`. Not worth optimizing initially. Path filtering in CI can be added later.\n   209→\n   210→3. **Lockfile churn**: The unified `bun.lock` will see more frequent changes because it covers both workspaces. Docs dependency updates will modify the lockfile even when no runtime code is affected. This is normal for monorepos and a minor inconvenience.\n   211→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"424193f8-5a8a-42b8-9942-76143e044b05","uuid":"1f60642c-ec33-40e9-bdb2-b3c74889590e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/rough-workspace/opus/addendum-tests.md","content":"# Addendum: Testing Considerations\n\n*Read alongside `plan.md`. Covers test impact, test patterns, and what to verify after the monorepo migration.*\n\n---\n\n## 1. What the supplementary materials reveal\n\n### Test infrastructure overview\n\nThe test suite is organized in four tiers:\n\n| Tier | Location | Runner | Count | External deps |\n|------|----------|--------|-------|--------------|\n| Unit | `tests/unit/` | `bun:test` | 65+ files | None |\n| Integration | `tests/integration/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Mock LLM |\n| E2E | `tests/e2e/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Real API keys |\n| Cross-runtime | `tests/cross-runtime/` | `bun`/`node`/`deno` | 3+ files | None |\n\nAll tests import from `../../server/<module>` using relative paths from within the `tests/` directory. Since the `server/` directory is not moving, **no test imports need to change**.\n\n### Test runner configuration\n\n- `bunfig.toml` sets `BUN_TEST=1` environment variable for test runs\n- `package.json` defines test scripts: `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `test`, `test:e2e:init`, `test:cross-runtime:*`\n- CI uses composite action `.github/actions/run-tests/action.yml` which calls `bun test tests/unit` and `bun test tests/integration`\n\n### Test utilities\n\nKey test utilities at `tests/utils/`:\n- `sentinel-test-harness.ts` — mock LLM calls, event tracking, test workspace management\n- `mock-llm.ts` — typed mock LLM provider with configurable responses\n- `env-test-helpers.ts` — environment variable capture/restore for test isolation\n\nNone of these reference paths outside the runtime package.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Existing tests affected by the planned changes\n\n### Directly affected: None\n\nNo existing test file needs modification. The migration changes:\n1. Root `package.json` (adds `workspaces` field)\n2. Scripts in `scripts/` (path adjustments)\n3. `.gitignore` (docs artifacts)\n4. SOP document\n\nNone of these are read by tests. The `tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts` reads from `schemas/` which is unchanged. The `tests/unit/config.test.ts` reads from `server/config.ts` which is unchanged.\n\n### Potentially affected (low risk)\n\n1. **`tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts`** — Tests that generated schemas validate correctly. The schemas themselves don't change, only where they're also copied to (now `docs/public/schemas/` instead of `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/`). The test reads from `schemas/` which is the runtime's local copy.\n\n2. **`tests/integration/schema-zod-parity.test.ts`** — Verifies Zod schemas match JSON schemas. Same as above — reads from `schemas/`, not affected.\n\n3. **Any test reading `package.json`** — The `\"workspaces\"` field addition shouldn't affect tests that read version or package name. Verified: `tests/unit/utils.test.ts` reads `getMetadata()` which extracts `name` and `version` from `package.json` — the `workspaces` field won't interfere.\n\n### Not affected: everything else\n\nAll unit tests, integration tests, E2E tests, and cross-runtime tests operate on runtime code and mock data. They have no awareness of the docs workspace.\n\n---\n\n## 3. New tests to write\n\n### No new automated tests are strictly required\n\nThe migration is a structural change (directory layout, workspace configuration) rather than a code change. The runtime behavior is identical before and after migration.\n\n### Recommended manual verification checklist\n\nAfter migration, verify by hand (or in a CI validation step):\n\n```bash\n# 1. Workspace installs correctly\nbun install\n# Expected: success, single bun.lock at root, docs/node_modules linked\n\n# 2. Runtime tests still pass\nbun run test:unit\nbun run test:integration\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\n\n# 3. Schema generation writes to both locations\nbun run generate-schemas\nls schemas/hank-file.schema.json\nls docs/public/schemas/hank-file.schema.json\n\n# 4. Runtime build works\nbun run build\nls dist/index.js\n\n# 5. Docs build works\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n\n# 6. npm pack excludes docs\nnpm pack --dry-run\n# Expected: docs/ NOT in the file list\n\n# 7. Sync dry-run strips docs correctly (requires git history)\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <version> --use-head\n# Expected: \"Correctly removed: docs\" in verification output\n```\n\n### Optional: Add a workspace smoke test\n\nIf desired, a lightweight test could be added to verify the monorepo structure is consistent:\n\n```typescript\n// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\nimport { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\n\ndescribe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n\n  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs schemas directory exists\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nThis is lightweight and validates the structural invariant. Optional — only add if the team wants structural tests.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Edge cases to cover\n\n### 4.1: `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI\n\nAfter migration, the CI composite action (`.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml:34`) runs:\n```bash\nbun install --frozen-lockfile\n```\n\nThis will fail if the `bun.lock` at root doesn't include the docs workspace's dependencies. **The `bun.lock` must be regenerated and committed as part of the migration.**\n\n### 4.2: The docs workspace's `devDependencies` in the root lockfile\n\nThe docs workspace has these dependencies that the runtime doesn't:\n- `next` ^15.0.0\n- `nextra` ^4.0.0\n- `nextra-theme-docs` ^4.0.0\n- `react` ^19.0.0\n- `react-dom` ^19.0.0\n- `@vercel/analytics` ^1.6.1\n- `posthog-js` ^1.347.2\n- `pagefind` ^1.3.0\n\nThese will be added to the root `bun.lock`. They should NOT conflict with the runtime's dependencies. The runtime doesn't use React or Next.js. The only shared dependency is `typescript` — both packages use it but can have independent versions.\n\n### 4.3: `npm publish` from root\n\nThe `release.yml` runs `npm publish` from the repo root. The `\"files\"` field in `package.json`:\n```json\n\"files\": [\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]\n```\n\nThis is an allowlist — `docs/` won't be included. Verify with `npm pack --dry-run` that the published tarball doesn't include docs workspace files.\n\n### 4.4: Build executable with workspace\n\n`build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and builds from root. Bun's build should resolve the entry point the same way with or without workspaces. Verify: `bun scripts/build-executable.ts` produces a working binary.\n\n### 4.5: Cross-runtime tests\n\n`scripts/run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. This path doesn't change. Cross-runtime tests import from `../../server/` which doesn't change. Should work without modification.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Test patterns and conventions to follow\n\nIf adding any new tests (e.g., the optional monorepo structure test):\n\n1. **Location**: `tests/unit/` for unit tests, `tests/integration/` for integration\n2. **Import style**: `import { ... } from \"bun:test\"` for test framework, `import * as fs from \"node:fs\"` for Node APIs\n3. **Relative imports**: `../../server/<module>` from test files\n4. **Cleanup**: Create temp directories, clean up in `afterEach`/`afterAll`\n5. **No global state**: Each test should be independent\n6. **Biome compliance**: Tests in `tests/unit/` and `tests/e2e/` are covered by Biome linting\n\n---\n\n## 6. Conflicts or inconsistencies\n\n**None identified.** The plan and test infrastructure are consistent. The migration doesn't touch any runtime code, so all existing tests should pass without modification.\n\nThe only \"inconsistency\" worth noting: the `generate-schemas.ts` script currently silently skips writing to docs if the path doesn't exist (`docsAvailable` check). After migration, this path will always exist, so the `docsAvailable` check becomes redundant. The plan recommends keeping the check (defensive) rather than removing it (premature cleanup).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Risks\n\n1. **Dependency hoisting conflicts**: Bun workspaces hoists dependencies. If the runtime and docs have conflicting versions of a shared transitive dependency, the hoist could cause issues. This is unlikely — the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees (server-side Bun tools vs. React/Next.js).\n\n2. **CI time increase**: CI now installs docs dependencies even when only runtime code changed. This adds maybe 10-20 seconds to `bun install`. Not worth optimizing initially. Path filtering in CI can be added later.\n\n3. **Lockfile churn**: The unified `bun.lock` will see more frequent changes because it covers both workspaces. Docs dependency updates will modify the lockfile even when no runtime code is affected. This is normal for monorepos and a minor inconvenience.\n","numLines":211,"startLine":1,"totalLines":211}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:39:30.094Z"}
